WEBVTT

1
00:01:19.047 --> 00:01:21.916
-(WOMAN GASPS)
-(TIRES SCREECHING)

2
00:01:21.983 --> 00:01:23.183
(SIGHS IN RELIEF)

3
00:01:29.256 --> 00:01:30.558
(TIRES SCREECHING)

4
00:01:34.829 --> 00:01:35.830
Oh, shit!

5
00:01:35.897 --> 00:01:36.898
(HORN BLARING)

6
00:01:38.165 --> 00:01:39.132
(PHONE CHIMES)

7
00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:44.438
Oh, fuck!

8
00:01:56.884 --> 00:01:59.119
(TIRES SCREECHING)

9
00:02:08.696 --> 00:02:10.665
<i>(THE NEW POLLUTION</i>
BY BECK PLAYING)

10
00:02:21.109 --> 00:02:23.544
This the line
for There Will Be Buns?

11
00:02:23.611 --> 00:02:25.379
You know it.

12
00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:27.015
Any idea how long
the wait's supposed to be?

13
00:02:27.081 --> 00:02:29.517
Uh, they said
about two hours.

14
00:02:29.584 --> 00:02:31.953
Wow. That's a long time
to wait for cinnamon buns.

15
00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:33.721
Is this your first bun?
They're incredible.

16
00:02:33.788 --> 00:02:35.590
I'm actually not
that big on sweets.

17
00:02:35.657 --> 00:02:37.357
Then why are you here?

18
00:02:38.225 --> 00:02:40.094
Oh, I'm on TaskSergeant.

19
00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.597
I'm actually getting paid to
wait in line for someone else.

20
00:02:42.664 --> 00:02:43.965
Hmm, that...

21
00:02:44.666 --> 00:02:46.199
sucks ass.

22
00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:47.334
Did you go to college?

23
00:02:47.401 --> 00:02:49.671
Uh, yeah, I went to college.

24
00:02:49.737 --> 00:02:51.438
Then why are you
a laundryman?

25
00:02:51.506 --> 00:02:53.875
I'm not a laundryman.
I'm doing TaskSergeant.

26
00:02:53.941 --> 00:02:56.511
Did you not do good
in college?

27
00:02:56.577 --> 00:02:59.047
ARJ: <i>Hey. Yeah, I'm still</i>
<i>waiting on those buns.</i>

28
00:02:59.113 --> 00:03:01.015
<i>They said it should probably</i>
<i>be another hour.</i>

29
00:03:01.082 --> 00:03:02.215
What do you want to be
when you grow up?

30
00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:03.618
I want to be an archeologist.

31
00:03:03.685 --> 00:03:05.053
ARJ: You want me to tell you
how that's going to go?

32
00:03:05.119 --> 00:03:06.621
You're going
to major in archeology,

33
00:03:06.688 --> 00:03:07.955
and then you're going
to get out

34
00:03:08.022 --> 00:03:10.758
and there's going to be
no archeology jobs.

35
00:03:10.825 --> 00:03:12.060
I've been an adult
a long time.

36
00:03:12.126 --> 00:03:13.928
You know how many
archeologists I've met?

37
00:03:13.995 --> 00:03:14.996
Zero.

38
00:03:16.964 --> 00:03:18.900
Okay, Arnold, meet...

39
00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:20.902
your new desk.

40
00:03:20.968 --> 00:03:23.638
<i>So now you got no job,</i>
<i>a useless degree,</i>

41
00:03:23.705 --> 00:03:24.939
and a ton of debt.

42
00:03:25.006 --> 00:03:26.273
What happens then?

43
00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:28.976
Well, I hope you like it here,
'cause guess what?

44
00:03:29.043 --> 00:03:30.078
You're moving back home!

45
00:03:30.144 --> 00:03:31.579
You need some money.

46
00:03:31.646 --> 00:03:33.280
<i>So you start</i>
<i>doing TaskSergeant.</i>

47
00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:35.382
<i>You take every part-time gig</i>
<i>you can get.</i>

48
00:03:35.449 --> 00:03:36.718
<i>You're working all the time.</i>

49
00:03:36.784 --> 00:03:38.385
<i>But you never have enough.</i>

50
00:03:38.452 --> 00:03:40.253
I know you got
a lot of big hopes.

51
00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.123
I used to be
a little Indian kid, too.

52
00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:44.291
But I got news for you,
little man.

53
00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:48.162
The American dream is dead.

54
00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:50.397
(PHONE CHIMES)

55
00:03:50.464 --> 00:03:52.734
Yeah, I probably shouldn't
have said that stuff.

56
00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.602
So sorry, guys.

57
00:03:54.669 --> 00:03:57.304
-All out for the day.
-MAN: What?

58
00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:00.340
I'm going to fuck this place
with one star.

59
00:04:00.407 --> 00:04:03.811
Hey, it's Arj
from TaskSergeant.

60
00:04:03.878 --> 00:04:08.015
Uh, I'm so sorry,
they actually sold out of buns.

61
00:04:08.082 --> 00:04:09.449
Yeah, you won't get charged
for the buns,

62
00:04:09.517 --> 00:04:11.686
but please don't
cancel the task.

63
00:04:11.753 --> 00:04:12.987
'Cause then I don't get paid,

64
00:04:13.054 --> 00:04:15.355
and, you know, I did
wait, like, two hours.

65
00:04:15.422 --> 00:04:18.593
Okay. Thanks
for understanding. Bye.

66
00:04:18.659 --> 00:04:20.327
-MAN: There are my buns!
-Hey.

67
00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:22.329
Yo. Thank you so much.

68
00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:24.132
-WOMAN: Sure.
-Ooh. The bag's still warm.

69
00:04:24.198 --> 00:04:27.334
-Love it. See you soon.
-See ya.

70
00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.036
Who's that guy?
How'd he get some buns?

71
00:04:29.103 --> 00:04:30.805
He's one of our investors.

72
00:04:30.872 --> 00:04:31.873
(PHONE CHIMES)

73
00:04:34.575 --> 00:04:35.676
Canceled? (GRUMBLES)

74
00:04:35.743 --> 00:04:37.645
You said you weren't
going to do that!

75
00:04:37.712 --> 00:04:38.980
Goddamn it, David H!

76
00:04:39.046 --> 00:04:40.882
(TSKS) Fuck my life.

77
00:04:56.197 --> 00:04:59.534
Hey. Can I talk
to you for a second?

78
00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:01.636
-ARJ: Sure.
-Elena from lumber.

79
00:05:01.702 --> 00:05:03.237
Arj, floor associate.

80
00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:06.007
-Sometimes power tools.
-(ELENA CHUCKLES)

81
00:05:06.073 --> 00:05:08.609
Are you happy with
the work environment here?

82
00:05:09.544 --> 00:05:10.578
No.

83
00:05:10.645 --> 00:05:12.547
Exactly.

84
00:05:12.613 --> 00:05:14.682
I mean, we know they can do
so much better here,

85
00:05:14.749 --> 00:05:17.417
(SOFTLY) and that's why
I'm trying to start a union.

86
00:05:17.484 --> 00:05:18.853
I'm just
working here part-time

87
00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.189
-to save some money
and then I'm moving on.
-Okay.

88
00:05:21.255 --> 00:05:22.757
Well, just because you're not
going to be somewhere forever

89
00:05:22.824 --> 00:05:24.625
doesn't mean
you can't make it better.

90
00:05:25.893 --> 00:05:26.861
Nothing ever changes.

91
00:05:27.995 --> 00:05:29.396
So what's your answer?

92
00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:30.598
Give up?

93
00:05:31.799 --> 00:05:34.202
-I don't have an answer.
-Hmm.

94
00:05:35.837 --> 00:05:40.473
Okay, Arj, floor associate,

95
00:05:42.009 --> 00:05:43.544
best of luck to you.

96
00:05:49.684 --> 00:05:50.685
Thank you.

97
00:05:52.753 --> 00:05:55.223
ELENA: Smelling good.

98
00:05:55.289 --> 00:05:58.793
Oh. You guys are
out of suadero. Damn!

99
00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:00.360
Suadero's my jam.

100
00:06:00.427 --> 00:06:03.598
Um, okay.
Have a good night.

101
00:06:03.664 --> 00:06:06.300
Hey. I got four.
You want some of mine?

102
00:06:07.668 --> 00:06:08.736
-Yeah.
-ARJ: All right.

103
00:06:08.803 --> 00:06:11.038
Come over here,
Elena from lumber.

104
00:06:11.105 --> 00:06:13.040
-You cool with these fixings?
-I am.

105
00:06:13.107 --> 00:06:14.275
I went a little heavy
on the green sauce.

106
00:06:14.342 --> 00:06:16.443
-Is that okay?
-That's always good.

107
00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:18.913
So how you been sleeping, man?
You look a little tired.

108
00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:20.948
Wow, thanks for noticing.

109
00:06:21.015 --> 00:06:22.216
It's a new look
I'm going for.

110
00:06:22.283 --> 00:06:23.584
Sorry.

111
00:06:23.651 --> 00:06:25.553
Uh, no, I haven't been
sleeping that well.

112
00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:27.755
-You got any tips?
-Actually, I do.

113
00:06:27.822 --> 00:06:29.090
I've been using
sleep stories

114
00:06:29.156 --> 00:06:30.457
-on my phone.
-Oh.

115
00:06:30.524 --> 00:06:31.893
Pretty much I just
listen to this guy talk,

116
00:06:31.959 --> 00:06:33.561
and he's so boring
that I just knock out.

117
00:06:33.628 --> 00:06:35.395
-I gotta give it a try.
-Works every time.

118
00:06:35.462 --> 00:06:37.164
So what do you do all day
when you're so well-rested?

119
00:06:38.465 --> 00:06:39.901
-I make furniture.
-Oh.

120
00:06:39.967 --> 00:06:41.602
Yeah, that's why I started
working at Hardware Heaven

121
00:06:41.669 --> 00:06:43.137
so I can get some
of those discounts.

122
00:06:43.204 --> 00:06:44.505
-Mmm.
-What about you?

123
00:06:44.572 --> 00:06:45.606
What do you do?

124
00:06:45.673 --> 00:06:46.974
Um, I'm an editor.

125
00:06:47.041 --> 00:06:49.310
I edit documentaries,
things like that.

126
00:06:49.377 --> 00:06:51.312
I love documentaries.
What you working on now?

127
00:06:51.379 --> 00:06:53.648
Right now, I'm just
doing freelance stuff.

128
00:06:53.714 --> 00:06:55.516
I'm hoping to get
another proper gig soon.

129
00:06:55.583 --> 00:06:57.752
You'll get another one.
Keep your dreams alive.

130
00:06:57.818 --> 00:06:58.953
ARJ: I once dated a girl

131
00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:00.420
that had that tattooed
on her lower back.

132
00:07:00.487 --> 00:07:01.656
ELENA: Oh, yeah?
Where is she now?

133
00:07:01.722 --> 00:07:03.057
ARJ: I think
she's dating this DJ.

134
00:07:03.124 --> 00:07:05.660
ANGEL: <i>Elena,</i>
<i>with the cinnamon bun guy?</i>

135
00:07:05.726 --> 00:07:07.494
ELENA: Have you
ever been to a rave?

136
00:07:07.561 --> 00:07:09.330
-ARJ: No, I haven't.
-Don't take the drugs.

137
00:07:09.397 --> 00:07:11.032
I think I'll just
take the drugs

138
00:07:11.098 --> 00:07:12.667
-and just not go to the rave.
-(ELENA LAUGHS)

139
00:07:12.733 --> 00:07:14.936
-What about that option?
-Love that.

140
00:07:15.002 --> 00:07:16.871
(ELENA LAUGHS)

141
00:07:35.022 --> 00:07:36.924
MAN: (OVER PHONE) <i>Hey,</i>
<i>how is the new apartment?</i>

142
00:07:38.125 --> 00:07:41.062
Um, it's cozy.

143
00:07:41.128 --> 00:07:44.532
<i>Great, great. I was</i>
<i>talking to Ayesha Auntie.</i>

144
00:07:44.598 --> 00:07:48.369
<i>Your little cousin Naveen</i>
<i>got a really good job</i>
<i>with Microsoft.</i>

145
00:07:48.436 --> 00:07:50.638
<i>He's making lot of money.</i>

146
00:07:50.705 --> 00:07:52.239
Good for Naveen.

147
00:07:52.306 --> 00:07:55.710
<i>Maybe he can help you</i>
<i>to get a job.</i>

148
00:07:55.776 --> 00:07:57.845
I'm an editor.
I work on documentaries.

149
00:07:57.912 --> 00:08:00.181
What am I going
to do at Microsoft?

150
00:08:00.247 --> 00:08:03.651
<i>Maybe you can do a documentary</i>
<i>about Naveen.</i>

151
00:08:03.718 --> 00:08:07.888
<i>He's very smart,</i>
<i>successful, well-dressed.</i>

152
00:08:07.955 --> 00:08:10.624
Okay. Um, well,
I'll think about it.

153
00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:15.396
WOMAN: (ON APP)
<i>Welcome to Sleep Town,</i>

154
00:08:15.463 --> 00:08:18.366
<i>the sleep assistance podcast.</i>

155
00:08:18.432 --> 00:08:24.772
<i>Now, slowly feel</i>
<i>each part of your body</i>
<i>shutting down for the day.</i>

156
00:08:24.839 --> 00:08:29.410
<i>Your feet, your lower legs,</i>
<i>your upper...</i>

157
00:08:29.477 --> 00:08:32.013
-(UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING)
-WOMAN: <i>Want to hear the pod</i>
<i>with no ads?</i>

158
00:08:32.079 --> 00:08:34.915
<i>Go to our channel</i>
<i>and subscribe now.</i>

159
00:08:34.982 --> 00:08:38.886
<i>Get exclusive sleep stories,</i>
<i>meditations and more.</i>

160
00:08:38.953 --> 00:08:40.821
<i>Only $5.99 a month.</i>

161
00:08:51.365 --> 00:08:53.901
All right. Everyone,
let's gather around.

162
00:09:09.784 --> 00:09:12.953
And there he was,
this lost soul,

163
00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:14.889
his head in his hands,

164
00:09:14.955 --> 00:09:18.759
about to jump headfirst
into Niagara Falls.

165
00:09:19.827 --> 00:09:22.296
As he lurked over the edge,

166
00:09:22.363 --> 00:09:24.765
panic filled his eyes
as he thought,

167
00:09:24.832 --> 00:09:28.803
"Oh, no. Is this the end?"

168
00:09:28.869 --> 00:09:31.772
I put my arm on his shoulder
and said,

169
00:09:31.839 --> 00:09:34.408
"Kenneth, I'm an angel.

170
00:09:34.475 --> 00:09:38.012
"My name is Azrael.
I'm here to save you."

171
00:09:38.079 --> 00:09:41.649
I showed him
what he had to live for.

172
00:09:41.715 --> 00:09:45.619
Visions that reflected
the hope his life promised.

173
00:09:45.686 --> 00:09:48.155
Cheering his son
at a soccer game,

174
00:09:48.222 --> 00:09:52.126
holding his wife on the couch
on a lazy Sunday,

175
00:09:52.193 --> 00:09:54.695
playing in the park
with his dog...

176
00:09:55.996 --> 00:09:58.332
Shoelace.

177
00:09:58.399 --> 00:10:02.303
"I see now that my life
was precious as it was.

178
00:10:02.369 --> 00:10:05.339
"Thank you
for showing me my path.

179
00:10:05.406 --> 00:10:08.543
"You are a special angel."

180
00:10:08.609 --> 00:10:11.580
(ALL APPLAUDING)

181
00:10:12.379 --> 00:10:14.115
GABRIEL: Martha?

182
00:10:14.181 --> 00:10:15.816
Yes, Gabriel.

183
00:10:15.883 --> 00:10:19.620
Is there any way I can
have more meaningful
duties like Azrael?

184
00:10:19.687 --> 00:10:21.355
I want to guide people,

185
00:10:21.422 --> 00:10:24.758
I want to change their lives,
I want to save a lost soul.

186
00:10:26.227 --> 00:10:30.297
To save a lost soul,
you have to find a lost soul.

187
00:10:30.364 --> 00:10:32.800
Finding a lost soul
is not easy, Gabriel.

188
00:10:32.867 --> 00:10:35.504
And showing them a path is...

189
00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:37.204
Is incredibly difficult.

190
00:10:37.271 --> 00:10:40.875
But I saw a person today.
His job is waiting in line.

191
00:10:40.941 --> 00:10:42.810
He's ready to give up
on his life.

192
00:10:42.877 --> 00:10:46.213
But that's not your task,
is it, Gabriel?

193
00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:48.182
How's the texting
and driving going?

194
00:10:48.249 --> 00:10:52.186
(SIGHS SOFTLY) It's a lot.
People really love doing it.

195
00:10:52.253 --> 00:10:53.988
What do you have this week?

196
00:10:54.054 --> 00:10:56.423
Um, I'm supposed to save
a woman named Elena,

197
00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:58.492
who works at a place
called Hardware Heaven.

198
00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:01.695
She almost backs
into a telephone pole.

199
00:11:01.762 --> 00:11:03.731
But you're not going to let
that happen, are you?

200
00:11:03.797 --> 00:11:05.866
No, I'm not.

201
00:11:05.933 --> 00:11:07.101
One step at a time.

202
00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:11.672
<i>(STREETS OF YOUR TOWN</i>
BY THE GO-BETWEENS PLAYING)

203
00:11:14.509 --> 00:11:16.043
Yeah. Uh...

204
00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:22.716
-(PA BUZZES)
-WOMAN ON PA: <i>Customer service</i>
<i>needed in plumbing.</i>

205
00:11:24.218 --> 00:11:26.020
<i>♪ Round and round ♪</i>

206
00:11:26.086 --> 00:11:27.488
<i>♪ Up and down ♪</i>

207
00:11:27.556 --> 00:11:29.957
<i>♪ Through the streets</i>
<i>of your town ♪</i>

208
00:11:30.024 --> 00:11:31.959
GUARD: Lot's for
customers only, sir.
You can't sleep here.

209
00:11:32.026 --> 00:11:34.695
ARJ: I know. I was just
about to go get some groceries.

210
00:11:34.762 --> 00:11:37.566
Really? Looks like
you covered up your windows
and went to sleep.

211
00:11:37.632 --> 00:11:38.966
I know that's what
it looks like, but...

212
00:11:39.033 --> 00:11:41.068
Don't let me catch you
out here again.

213
00:11:41.135 --> 00:11:42.469
Okay.

214
00:11:42.537 --> 00:11:43.672
<i>♪ And don't the sun</i>
<i>look good today? ♪</i>

215
00:11:45.039 --> 00:11:47.542
<i>♪ Shine ♪</i>

216
00:11:47.609 --> 00:11:50.411
<i>♪ But the rain is on its way ♪</i>

217
00:11:52.379 --> 00:11:54.782
<i>♪ Shine ♪</i>

218
00:11:54.848 --> 00:11:59.286
<i>♪ Watch the butcher shine</i>
<i>his knives ♪</i>

219
00:11:59.353 --> 00:12:02.156
Yo, Arj, my Indian brother.
What's going on, man?

220
00:12:02.223 --> 00:12:03.958
Hey, what's up, Leonard?

221
00:12:04.024 --> 00:12:06.293
You know, you don't have
to mention I'm Indian
every time you say hi.

222
00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:08.262
Oh, my bad.
You Pakistani?

223
00:12:08.329 --> 00:12:10.164
Just forget about it.

224
00:12:10.231 --> 00:12:12.433
-Uh, you good?
-Yo, quick favor.

225
00:12:12.499 --> 00:12:15.002
You got some toothpaste
I could borrow? I'm all out.

226
00:12:15.069 --> 00:12:16.737
ARJ: Uh, yeah.

227
00:12:16.804 --> 00:12:18.506
-Here you go.
-Oh, thanks.

228
00:12:18.573 --> 00:12:20.808
Oh, you don't have the one
with the little whitening
crystals, do you?

229
00:12:20.874 --> 00:12:22.276
I got a big date tonight.

230
00:12:22.343 --> 00:12:24.111
No, sorry. What's up
with this big date?

231
00:12:24.178 --> 00:12:28.249
Oh, yo, this girl Susan,
she works at the CVS
up in Burbank.

232
00:12:28.315 --> 00:12:31.852
I asked, I said,
"Yo, why you smell
like blueberries?"

233
00:12:31.919 --> 00:12:33.320
And now,
we're going on a date.

234
00:12:33.387 --> 00:12:34.755
-That worked?
-Hell, yeah.

235
00:12:34.822 --> 00:12:37.592
Dude, girls love it
