the ribeye, it's great.

474
00:21:47.440 --> 00:21:50.211
So let's talk
about the ensemble.

475
00:21:50.278 --> 00:21:52.412
Is this what we're, uh,
wearing on our date?

476
00:21:52.479 --> 00:21:53.948
The coffee stain
and all that?

477
00:21:54.782 --> 00:21:55.950
I guess.

478
00:21:57.051 --> 00:21:58.653
My little jacket.

479
00:21:58.719 --> 00:22:00.121
I got this little jacket.

480
00:22:00.188 --> 00:22:02.023
I bought it a while ago,
and I haven't returned it.

481
00:22:02.089 --> 00:22:03.758
It's a little teensy on me,

482
00:22:03.825 --> 00:22:05.392
but it could be
perfect on you.

483
00:22:05.458 --> 00:22:07.028
Yeah, you can borrow it
for the date.

484
00:22:07.094 --> 00:22:08.095
All right.

485
00:22:08.162 --> 00:22:09.931
-Yeah.
-Ooh, it's nice!

486
00:22:09.997 --> 00:22:11.132
Like a glove.

487
00:22:11.199 --> 00:22:13.134
I feel like Kevin James
in <i>Hitch.</i>

488
00:22:13.201 --> 00:22:15.670
That makes me Hitch in <i>Hitch.</i>

489
00:22:15.736 --> 00:22:17.772
Hah. He's a cool guy.
Thank you.

490
00:22:17.839 --> 00:22:20.241
-I like your jacket.
-Oh, thanks.

491
00:22:20.308 --> 00:22:22.076
-You look very nice, too.
-Thanks.

492
00:22:22.143 --> 00:22:23.744
Um, I'm so glad
we did this.

493
00:22:23.811 --> 00:22:26.379
-Me, too.
-Yeah.

494
00:22:26.446 --> 00:22:27.849
At first,
I kinda hated you.

495
00:22:27.915 --> 00:22:29.349
-What? What did I do?
-Yeah.

496
00:22:29.416 --> 00:22:30.551
I mean, you were
just so, like,

497
00:22:30.618 --> 00:22:31.953
(IN A DRAB VOICE)
"I don't believe in much."

498
00:22:32.019 --> 00:22:33.386
I... Oh, come on.

499
00:22:33.453 --> 00:22:34.956
-I didn't talk like that.
-Yeah. You did.

500
00:22:35.022 --> 00:22:36.224
(IN A DRAB VOICE)
"Oh, I don't know."

501
00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:38.726
-No. Come on.
-You did. Yeah, that was you.

502
00:22:38.793 --> 00:22:40.127
And now, look at you.

503
00:22:40.194 --> 00:22:41.262
Hey, guys,
how are we tonight?

504
00:22:41.329 --> 00:22:43.231
-Hey, how are you?
-Good, thank you.

505
00:22:43.297 --> 00:22:44.899
Thank you. So what are we
thinking food-wise?

506
00:22:44.966 --> 00:22:46.901
ARJ: My friend said
we definitely have
to get a ribeye.

507
00:22:46.968 --> 00:22:48.368
ELENA: It does
look very good.

508
00:22:48.435 --> 00:22:49.637
Oh, it's a signature dish.

509
00:22:49.704 --> 00:22:50.805
They grill it right
on the fire. It's so good.

510
00:22:50.872 --> 00:22:52.273
-ARJ: All right.
-Cool.

511
00:22:52.340 --> 00:22:54.242
-Cool.
-Thanks.

512
00:22:54.308 --> 00:22:57.144
-So we usually say about three
to four plates per person.
-ELENA: All right.

513
00:22:57.211 --> 00:22:58.913
WAITRESS:
Everything is shared,
family style.

514
00:22:58.980 --> 00:23:00.715
And we have
some amazing wines,

515
00:23:00.781 --> 00:23:02.449
if you want to talk
to our sommelier about it.

516
00:23:02.516 --> 00:23:03.718
-Okay.
-WAITRESS: Cool.

517
00:23:03.784 --> 00:23:05.086
-I'll give you guys a minute.
-Thanks.

518
00:23:05.152 --> 00:23:06.621
Welcome.

519
00:23:06.687 --> 00:23:09.223
I am so good
without the ribeye.

520
00:23:09.290 --> 00:23:11.659
-Yeah, it's a big steak.
-(ELENA CHUCKLES)

521
00:23:11.726 --> 00:23:12.760
Maybe we do the trout.

522
00:23:12.827 --> 00:23:14.729
-Trout sounds perfect.
-Yeah.

523
00:23:14.795 --> 00:23:17.131
I'm actually super easy,
and they said everything's
meant to be shared.

524
00:23:17.198 --> 00:23:18.566
-So let's share.
-Yeah. Let's share,

525
00:23:18.633 --> 00:23:20.067
-family style.
-Yeah.

526
00:23:20.134 --> 00:23:21.335
It's a small family,
just the two of us.

527
00:23:21.401 --> 00:23:23.104
No kids.

528
00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:25.438
I'm telling you,
I used to kill it in
my school talent shows.

529
00:23:25.506 --> 00:23:26.941
Really?
What was your talent?

530
00:23:27.008 --> 00:23:29.277
Singing, dancing,
everything.

531
00:23:29.343 --> 00:23:31.646
-Oh. What'd you sing?
-Mmm.

532
00:23:31.712 --> 00:23:33.314
Hey, team. Here's the bill
whenever you're ready.

533
00:23:33.381 --> 00:23:35.082
-Thanks.
-You're welcome.

534
00:23:37.184 --> 00:23:38.451
ELENA: Wow. We should
definitely split this.

535
00:23:38.519 --> 00:23:40.521
No, no, no. I'll get it.

536
00:23:40.588 --> 00:23:42.757
-ELENA: You sure?
-Yeah, yeah.

537
00:23:42.823 --> 00:23:45.259
Don't worry about it.
My treat.

538
00:23:45.326 --> 00:23:47.695
ELENA: Thank you.
This was...

539
00:23:47.762 --> 00:23:48.796
This was so lovely.

540
00:24:13.421 --> 00:24:14.588
JEFF: Hey, Arj?

541
00:24:15.556 --> 00:24:17.291
Hey. You get my email?

542
00:24:17.358 --> 00:24:19.694
Are you all set
for ayahuasca tonight?

543
00:24:19.760 --> 00:24:21.228
Yeah. Um...

544
00:24:23.230 --> 00:24:27.134
Did you use my card
to buy yourself dinner
last night?

545
00:24:27.201 --> 00:24:29.003
I... I talked to your
accountant about that.

546
00:24:29.070 --> 00:24:30.571
I... I'm gonna pay you back
right away.

547
00:24:30.638 --> 00:24:32.974
I just got in a little bit
of a jam at Dunsmoor,

548
00:24:33.040 --> 00:24:34.742
and the waitress recommended
an expensive bottle of wine.

549
00:24:34.809 --> 00:24:35.910
I didn't know what to do.

550
00:24:35.977 --> 00:24:38.212
-You can't do that.
-I totally get that.

551
00:24:38.279 --> 00:24:39.714
It won't happen again.

552
00:24:39.780 --> 00:24:41.382
And I'm gonna pay you back
as soon as I can.

553
00:24:41.449 --> 00:24:43.184
I'm really sorry.

554
00:24:43.250 --> 00:24:46.087
Um, we need to stop
working together,
unfortunately.

555
00:24:48.222 --> 00:24:50.725
-Really?
-Yeah.

556
00:24:50.791 --> 00:24:52.059
I mean, I'm gonna
pay you back, man.

557
00:24:52.126 --> 00:24:54.528
You told me to go there.
You said it wasn't pricey.

558
00:24:54.595 --> 00:24:56.430
Just don't
make it weird, okay?

559
00:24:56.496 --> 00:24:59.033
Just, thank you for everything,
and I'm really sorry.

560
00:25:00.968 --> 00:25:02.303
Um, I'm sorry, too.

561
00:25:15.016 --> 00:25:17.051
"Currently full"?

562
00:25:17.118 --> 00:25:18.119
(SIGHS)

563
00:25:25.159 --> 00:25:26.727
-WOMAN: Have you
done this before?
-ARJ: No.

564
00:25:26.794 --> 00:25:29.897
Whole process takes
about an hour and a half
to two hours.

565
00:25:29.964 --> 00:25:31.098
TAMMY: Tonight,
we're gonna be working

566
00:25:31.165 --> 00:25:34.969
with magic mushrooms
and ayahuasca.

567
00:25:35.036 --> 00:25:36.637
All right, the needle's
gonna go right here.

568
00:25:48.382 --> 00:25:50.351
(RETCHING)

569
00:25:52.053 --> 00:25:53.154
(GROANS)

570
00:25:56.157 --> 00:25:57.258
(LAUGHS)

571
00:25:57.324 --> 00:25:59.026
(RETCHING)

572
00:25:59.827 --> 00:26:01.829
(PANTING)

573
00:26:10.805 --> 00:26:11.939
MAN: Yo.

574
00:26:12.006 --> 00:26:13.607
Get your lil' ass up.

575
00:26:13.674 --> 00:26:16.010
You can't be sleeping
in no Denny's, man.

576
00:26:16.077 --> 00:26:17.411
-I'm sorry.
-And them outlets are off.

577
00:26:17.478 --> 00:26:19.346
You ain't getting no juice
to your phone.

578
00:26:27.888 --> 00:26:29.524
Hey!

579
00:26:29.590 --> 00:26:31.692
Did you see a Golf
parked out here?

580
00:26:31.759 --> 00:26:33.627
The one with the duct tape
on the bumper?

581
00:26:33.694 --> 00:26:35.629
-Yeah.
-It got towed.

582
00:26:35.696 --> 00:26:37.631
Towed? Why'd it get towed?

583
00:26:37.698 --> 00:26:39.133
I don't know.

584
00:26:39.200 --> 00:26:41.836
Am I dressed like a cop
or a guy that works at Denny's?

585
00:26:41.902 --> 00:26:42.903
Denny's.

586
00:26:44.506 --> 00:26:45.639
(SIGHS)

587
00:26:45.706 --> 00:26:46.941
Parking tickets.

588
00:26:48.075 --> 00:26:49.877
MAN: Yeah, that'll do it.

589
00:26:49.944 --> 00:26:51.712
They gonna charge you for
the tickets and for the tow.

590
00:26:51.779 --> 00:26:53.180
I'm sorry.

591
00:26:53.247 --> 00:26:54.516
If I knew your night
was going like this,

592
00:26:54.583 --> 00:26:56.150
I'd have let you sleep
some more, man.

593
00:27:04.758 --> 00:27:06.227
(SIGHS)

594
00:27:16.904 --> 00:27:18.806
His head's in his hands.

595
00:27:20.241 --> 00:27:21.408
I knew it.

596
00:27:22.977 --> 00:27:25.514
A lost soul.

597
00:27:27.915 --> 00:27:30.885
Arj, I'm an angel.
My name is Gabriel.

598
00:27:30.951 --> 00:27:32.186
I'm here to save you.

599
00:27:33.588 --> 00:27:34.755
What?

600
00:27:34.822 --> 00:27:36.857
Who the fuck are you?
How do you know my name?

601
00:27:38.893 --> 00:27:40.394
Maybe you don't understand.

602
00:27:40.461 --> 00:27:42.730
I'm an angel.

603
00:27:42.796 --> 00:27:45.032
See the wings?

604
00:27:45.099 --> 00:27:47.434
I've been observing you.
I know all about you.

605
00:27:47.501 --> 00:27:49.504
I know you're living
in your car.

606
00:27:49.571 --> 00:27:51.839
I know you lost
your job with Jeff.

607
00:27:51.906 --> 00:27:54.175
-What?
-I even know that right now

608
00:27:54.241 --> 00:27:55.242
there's a part
of you that thinks

609
00:27:55.309 --> 00:27:56.911
your life
isn't worth living.

610
00:27:56.977 --> 00:27:58.913
But it's not true.

611
00:27:58.979 --> 00:28:01.550
You have so much
to live for.

612
00:28:01.616 --> 00:28:03.150
Let me show you.

613
00:28:06.120 --> 00:28:08.590
Holy shit!
What happened?

614
00:28:08.657 --> 00:28:10.057
What is this?
Where are we?

615
00:28:10.124 --> 00:28:14.261
Visions that reflect the hope
your life promises.

616
00:28:14.328 --> 00:28:18.533
I know you've been having
trouble finding work now,
but look.

617
00:28:21.468 --> 00:28:24.071
I get a job driving one
of those delivery trucks?

618
00:28:24.138 --> 00:28:25.873
-Yes.
-MAN: Hey, Arj.

619
00:28:25.940 --> 00:28:27.474
Don't forget
your pee bottle, bro.

620
00:28:28.809 --> 00:28:30.545
Why do I need
a pee bottle?

621
00:28:30.612 --> 00:28:32.112
Your deadlines
are very strict

622
00:28:32.179 --> 00:28:34.381
and you don't have time
for bathroom breaks.

623
00:28:34.448 --> 00:28:36.350
Hence the pee bottle.

624
00:28:37.985 --> 00:28:38.986
Okay.

625
00:28:39.053 --> 00:28:41.255
But wait, there's more.

626
00:28:44.725 --> 00:28:48.495
I know you're living
in your car now, but look.

627
00:28:48.563 --> 00:28:50.599
Elena and I
move in together?

628
00:28:50.665 --> 00:28:53.133
Um, technically, you both
move in with her mom.

629
00:28:53.200 --> 00:28:55.769
Elena, Darryl and Mercedes
are coming over again.

630
00:28:55.836 --> 00:28:57.771
So could you two sleep
in the living room?

631
00:28:57.838 --> 00:28:59.306
And fold the couch bed up
in the morning, please.

632
00:28:59.373 --> 00:29:00.675
Yes, yes, Ma.

633
00:29:00.741 --> 00:29:03.077
Hey, has anyone seen
my air fryer? I can't find it.

634
00:29:03.143 --> 00:29:05.946
For the millionth time, Jay,
I didn't use your air fryer.

635
00:29:06.013 --> 00:29:07.748
I'm just eating spaghetti,
minding my business.

636
00:29:07.815 --> 00:29:09.183
Fuck it.

637
00:29:09.250 --> 00:29:10.818
Who's that guy?

638
00:29:10.884 --> 00:29:14.021
It's her sister
Patrice's on-and-off-again
boyfriend, Jay.

639
00:29:14.088 --> 00:29:16.123
-They live here, too.
-JAY: Arj,

640
00:29:16.190 --> 00:29:17.458
have you been
using my body wash?

641
00:29:17.525 --> 00:29:18.826
I'm missing some body wash.

642
00:29:18.892 --> 00:29:20.828
Seems a bit crowded.

643
00:29:20.894 --> 00:29:25.899
But you both
eventually get steady jobs
and move to Texas.

644
00:29:30.371 --> 00:29:31.839
FUTURE ARJ: Hey.

645
00:29:31.905 --> 00:29:33.841
So what'd they say?

646
00:29:33.907 --> 00:29:35.976
He's gonna have
to have the surgery.

647
00:29:36.043 --> 00:29:37.612
Okay, how much is it?

648
00:29:37.679 --> 00:29:39.547
We can't afford it.

649
00:29:39.614 --> 00:29:41.448
Then what's gonna
happen to Dapper?

650
00:29:41.516 --> 00:29:42.883
Does that mean
we're gonna have to...

651
00:29:42.950 --> 00:29:44.151
Oh.

652
00:29:44.218 --> 00:29:46.153
Oh, no.

653
00:29:46.220 --> 00:29:48.690
I'm so sorry, buddy.

654
00:29:48.757 --> 00:29:51.458
We have to put
the dog to sleep?

655
00:29:51.526 --> 00:29:53.227
Yes.

656
00:29:53.294 --> 00:29:54.663
Let's maybe
get out of here.

657
00:29:56.363 --> 00:29:58.566
That's what I have
to live for?

658
00:29:58.633 --> 00:30:01.802
Yeah. What's wrong?
Why are you so upset?

659
00:30:01.869 --> 00:30:03.370
Because my life sucks!

660
00:30:03.437 --> 00:30:07.141
I mean, it's not the
worst life in the world,
but damn, man.

661
00:30:07.207 --> 00:30:09.376
Pee bottle? Dead dog?

662
00:30:09.443 --> 00:30:10.745
I did everything
I was supposed to do,

663
00:30:10.811 --> 00:30:12.179
and nothing's working out.

664
00:30:13.947 --> 00:30:16.551
I'm going to be honest
with you, Arj.

665
00:30:16.618 --> 00:30:19.153
I'm not really supposed
to be doing this.

666
00:30:19.219 --> 00:30:20.220
What does that mean?

667
00:30:20.287 --> 00:30:23.692
I'm overstepping
my bounds as an angel.

668
00:30:23.758 --> 00:30:26.193
Do you see how my wings
are kind of small?

669
00:30:26.260 --> 00:30:27.529
I wasn't gonna
say anything,

670
00:30:27.595 --> 00:30:29.531
but yeah,
they're on the tinier side.

671
00:30:29.597 --> 00:30:32.099
It means I'm lower order.

672
00:30:32.166 --> 00:30:33.367
I'm normally only in charge

673
00:30:33.434 --> 00:30:35.869
of saving people
from texting and driving.

674
00:30:35.936 --> 00:30:39.541
Wait. You're telling me I have
a budget guardian angel?

675
00:30:39.607 --> 00:30:42.209
-Kinda.
-(SIGHS)

676
00:30:42.276 --> 00:30:43.944
I'm just trying
to help you.

677
00:30:44.011 --> 00:30:45.747
I want you to have hope.

678
00:30:45.814 --> 00:30:49.350
I need to show you
that your life is precious,

679
00:30:49.416 --> 00:30:51.519
that it's worth living.

680
00:30:51.586 --> 00:30:53.120
My life isn't precious.

681
00:30:53.187 --> 00:30:56.090
My life is just in the service
of people like Jeff,

682
00:30:56.156 --> 00:30:57.592
the people
who actually get to live

683
00:30:57.659 --> 00:31:00.861
and go on vacations
and do cold plunges.

684
00:31:00.928 --> 00:31:04.666
You think Jeff's life is
the life that's worth living?

685
00:31:06.033 --> 00:31:09.103
Maybe I can show you
that that life

686
00:31:09.169 --> 00:31:11.573
is not all
it's cracked up to be.

687
00:31:13.842 --> 00:31:14.843
(TAPPING ON CAR WINDOW)

688
00:31:17.945 --> 00:31:19.079
GUARD: Sir?

689
00:31:22.449 --> 00:31:24.451
Sir, are you okay?

690
00:31:24.519 --> 00:31:26.453
What?

691
00:31:26.521 --> 00:31:28.422
You must've fallen asleep
in your car. (CHUCKLES)

692
00:31:28.489 --> 00:31:31.959
Yeah, I fell asleep.

693
00:31:32.025 --> 00:31:34.461
No problem.
Get home safe, okay?

694
00:31:34.529 --> 00:31:35.929
Okay.

695
00:31:41.736 --> 00:31:43.070
FEMALE AUTOMATED VOICE:
<i>Good morning, Arj.</i>

696
00:31:43.137 --> 00:31:46.073
<i>Would you like to go home?</i>

697
00:31:46.140 --> 00:31:47.474
<i>Navigating to home.</i>

698
00:31:47.542 --> 00:31:51.178
<i>Estimated drive time,</i>
<i>one hour and ten minutes.</i>

699
00:32:28.683 --> 00:32:30.117
ARJ: Jeff?

700
00:32:31.285 --> 00:32:33.053
JEFF: Yo!

701
00:32:33.120 --> 00:32:35.857
I was just upstairs unloading
some packages that came in.

702
00:32:35.924 --> 00:32:37.625
Those house slippers
you wanted arrived.

703
00:32:37.692 --> 00:32:39.126
They're very cool.

704
00:32:40.194 --> 00:32:42.831
-What are you doing?
-Nothing.

705
00:32:42.897 --> 00:32:45.199
You good?
You need anything?

706
00:32:45.265 --> 00:32:48.670
-No, I'm good.
-All right.

707
00:32:48.736 --> 00:32:51.371
Uh, I'm gonna
go finish up.

708
00:32:51.438 --> 00:32:54.475
Just let me know
if you want anything, okay?

709
00:32:56.443 --> 00:32:58.078
-Uh, hey, Jeff.
-Yeah?

710
00:33:00.214 --> 00:33:01.749
Whose house is this?

711
00:33:03.217 --> 00:33:05.419
Your house. (CHUCKLES)

712
00:33:25.807 --> 00:33:27.609
Enjoying your new life?

713
00:33:27.675 --> 00:33:28.943
What's happened?

714
00:33:29.009 --> 00:33:31.713
You wanted to have wealth
and success, here you go.

715
00:33:31.779 --> 00:33:33.046
Take a good look around,

716
00:33:33.113 --> 00:33:35.750
see if Jeff's life is
all it's cracked up to be.

717
00:33:35.817 --> 00:33:36.951
I'll check in on you,

718
00:33:37.017 --> 00:33:38.385
and at the end of the week,
we'll assess.

719
00:33:38.452 --> 00:33:40.354
-But I'm still me?
-Yes.

720
00:33:40.420 --> 00:33:43.023
Your name is Arj,
you look like you,

721
00:33:43.090 --> 00:33:46.260
but everything else
is Jeff's life.

722
00:33:46.326 --> 00:33:49.429
Both the good
and the bad.

723
00:33:49.496 --> 00:33:50.899
What happened to Jeff?

724
00:33:50.965 --> 00:33:53.635
He has your life.
He thinks he's you.

725
00:33:53.701 --> 00:33:55.235
So he's my assistant?

726
00:33:55.302 --> 00:33:56.704
Yes.

727
00:33:56.771 --> 00:33:57.972
So he has to do
whatever I ask him to do?

728
00:33:58.673 --> 00:33:59.707
Yes.

729
00:33:59.774 --> 00:34:01.074
If I'm hungry
and I want a snack?

730
00:34:01.141 --> 00:34:03.143
GABRIEL:
He'll get it for you.

731
00:34:03.210 --> 00:34:04.378
Hey, Jeff!

732
00:34:04.444 --> 00:34:06.881
Chips and guac
coming right up.

733
00:34:06.948 --> 00:34:08.616
My man!

734
00:34:08.683 --> 00:34:09.984
JEFF: I'm just gonna
head upstairs to your room,

735
00:34:10.050 --> 00:34:11.251
and finish unpacking
those clothes.

736
00:34:11.318 --> 00:34:12.620
All right, cool.

737
00:34:12.687 --> 00:34:14.822
Enjoying the pool?

738
00:34:14.889 --> 00:34:17.324
Gabriel, the angel!
Can Jeff see you?

739
00:34:17.391 --> 00:34:18.993
No, only you can see me.

740
00:34:19.059 --> 00:34:22.262
Ah. Well, I got to say,
so far, this is great.

741
00:34:22.329 --> 00:34:23.998
You want to hit the pool?
Pop on some trunks?

742
00:34:24.064 --> 00:34:26.000
Hey, Arj, uh,
just reminding you,

743
00:34:26.066 --> 00:34:27.401
you got this meeting
coming up.

744
00:34:27.467 --> 00:34:29.136
You should probably
get ready to go soon.

745
00:34:29.202 --> 00:34:30.838
Meeting?

746
00:34:30.905 --> 00:34:31.973
I don't know
anything about his work.

747
00:34:32.040 --> 00:34:33.140
What am I gonna say?

748
00:34:33.206 --> 00:34:35.977
You wanted to see
what this life is like.

749
00:34:36.044 --> 00:34:39.279
Time to get to work,
Mr. Mogul.

750
00:34:39.346 --> 00:34:40.682
-That's for you.
-ARJ: Oh, God.

751
00:34:40.748 --> 00:34:42.550
There we go,
bon appe-fucking-tit.

752
00:34:46.253 --> 00:34:47.487
Oh, my God!

753
00:34:47.555 --> 00:34:50.024
-This sushi's insane!
-So sick, right?

754
00:34:50.090 --> 00:34:52.660
They fly the fish in
from Japan every morning.

755
00:34:52.727 --> 00:34:54.294
Very high carbon footprint.

756
00:34:54.361 --> 00:34:55.697
-That's awesome.
-Yeah.

757
00:34:55.763 --> 00:34:57.031
Yo, did you check out
that launch proposal

758
00:34:57.097 --> 00:34:58.198
I sent over
for the event next week?

759
00:34:58.265 --> 00:34:59.366
What'd you think
about that?

760
00:34:59.834 --> 00:35:00.835
Uh...

761
00:35:00.902 --> 00:35:02.269
"Uh..."

762
00:35:02.336 --> 00:35:04.038
Looked good, I guess.

763
00:35:04.104 --> 00:35:06.808
Yeah? Great.

764
00:35:06.874 --> 00:35:08.442
All right. Well, yeah,
that's all the business

765
00:35:08.509 --> 00:35:10.511
we had to get to today.
So, what the fuck? How's life?

766
00:35:10.578 --> 00:35:13.815
Uh, same old. Just working,
cold plunging. You?

767
00:35:13.881 --> 00:35:15.215
Work has been crazy, man.

768
00:35:15.282 --> 00:35:17.150
I had to fire one
of my assistants, Darren.

769
00:35:17.217 --> 00:35:18.485
-Oh.
-Yeah, he's a sweetheart.

770
00:35:18.553 --> 00:35:20.888
But I had this big event
in New York last week

771
00:35:20.955 --> 00:35:22.456
and I put him
in charge of vibes.

772
00:35:22.523 --> 00:35:24.324
And then I get there,
and the vibes are
just super off.

773
00:35:24.391 --> 00:35:25.392
-Hate that.
-Yeah.

774
00:35:25.459 --> 00:35:27.127
-Wrong kind of candles.
-Oh.

775
00:35:27.194 --> 00:35:29.329
He didn't tag
the liquor sponsor
in the media posts.

776
00:35:29.396 --> 00:35:31.198
-No!
-The event was off a cliff.

777
00:35:31.264 --> 00:35:33.067
-The vibes were just tanked.
-What was the scent

778
00:35:33.133 --> 00:35:34.736
he was supposed to get
and what did he grab instead?

779
00:35:34.802 --> 00:35:35.870
He was supposed
to get sandalwood.

780
00:35:35.937 --> 00:35:37.005
-He got vetiver.
-Ugh!

781
00:35:37.071 --> 00:35:38.573
Whole place
smelled like shit.

782
00:35:38.640 --> 00:35:40.074
Those aren't the same smells.

783
00:35:40.140 --> 00:35:41.475
-Everybody at the event
must've been furious.
-Yeah.

784
00:35:41.542 --> 00:35:43.044
But you know
what though, dude?

785
00:35:43.111 --> 00:35:46.213
I've been reading a lot about,
like, empathy and forgiveness

786
00:35:46.279 --> 00:35:48.382
in this new Jay Shetty book,
so blessings to Darren.

787
00:35:48.448 --> 00:35:50.317
Ah, thank you.
Hey, let me get this.

788
00:35:50.384 --> 00:35:52.754
Dude, no. Put it
on the company.

789
00:35:52.820 --> 00:35:54.856
It was a "business lunch"
after all, right?

790
00:35:54.922 --> 00:35:57.190
(LAUGHS) Oh, yeah.
Why would we pay?

791
00:35:57.257 --> 00:36:00.193
This was the best lunch
I've ever had!

792
00:36:00.260 --> 00:36:02.195
MAN: Thank you. All right,
we got to go, though.

793
00:36:02.262 --> 00:36:04.398
I got to hit the cardio store,
get a couple nibbles.

794
00:36:04.464 --> 00:36:06.868
<i>(DO YOU WANNA FUNK</i>
BY PATRICK COWLEY PLAYING)

795
00:36:12.073 --> 00:36:13.173
MAN: Excuse me, sir.

796
00:36:13.240 --> 00:36:14.742
ARJ: Oh, hi.
Can I help you?

797
00:36:14.809 --> 00:36:17.444
Yeah, I'm Grant. You called me
to check out the pool heater.

798
00:36:17.512 --> 00:36:19.279
Ooh, that's right.
What's the deal?

799
00:36:19.346 --> 00:36:20.948
So, bad news,
the heater's busted.

800
00:36:21.015 --> 00:36:22.215
Probably gonna have
to replace it.

801
00:36:22.282 --> 00:36:23.851
Probably like 30K
for the heater,

802
00:36:23.918 --> 00:36:26.020
another five
for the install.

803
00:36:26.087 --> 00:36:27.121
Okay.

804
00:36:28.523 --> 00:36:30.625
Problems with your home?

805
00:36:30.692 --> 00:36:35.029
Some pretty serious expenses.
Must be inconvenient.

806
00:36:35.096 --> 00:36:36.564
Good thing I got
a shit ton of money

807
00:36:36.631 --> 00:36:39.299
to cover any and all problems
that come my way. (CHUCKLES)

808
00:36:39.366 --> 00:36:40.601
See you later, Gabe.

809
00:36:40.668 --> 00:36:42.537
I'm off to the sauna.

810
00:36:42.603 --> 00:36:43.938
<i>♪ There is something ♪</i>

811
00:36:44.005 --> 00:36:45.807
ARJ: So she doesn't
remember me at all?

812
00:36:45.873 --> 00:36:48.609
This version of you
didn't exist until today.

813
00:36:48.676 --> 00:36:52.180
So you'll have
to reintroduce yourself.

814
00:36:52.245 --> 00:36:54.381
<i>♪ ...that I want to know ♪</i>

815
00:36:54.448 --> 00:36:55.415
Okay.

816
00:36:56.884 --> 00:36:58.351
Elena from lumber.

817
00:36:59.187 --> 00:37:00.755
Uh, yeah.

818
00:37:00.822 --> 00:37:02.724
You helped me find some lumber
one time. It was very helpful.

819
00:37:02.790 --> 00:37:04.659
Oh, well,
I'm glad it worked out.

820
00:37:04.726 --> 00:37:05.993
ARJ: How's it going
over there?

821
00:37:06.060 --> 00:37:07.061
ELENA: In lumber?

822
00:37:08.162 --> 00:37:09.630
It's good.

823
00:37:09.697 --> 00:37:12.633
I'm glad. I was just over
in plumbing, it's a shit show.

824
00:37:12.700 --> 00:37:15.002
-(CHUCKLES)
-I'm Arj.

825
00:37:16.303 --> 00:37:17.739
Nice to meet you, Arj.

826
00:37:17.805 --> 00:37:20.575
<i>♪ If you wanna funk,</i>
<i>let me show you how ♪</i>

827
00:37:20.641 --> 00:37:21.743
(INAUDIBLE)

828
00:37:21.809 --> 00:37:24.746
<i>♪ Do you wanna funk with me? ♪</i>

829
00:37:24.812 --> 00:37:26.514
Do we have any thoughts
food-wise?

830
00:37:26.581 --> 00:37:28.616
Uh, I mean, we were
looking at the ribeye.

831
00:37:28.683 --> 00:37:30.785
-It does look very good.
-Let's do it.

832
00:37:32.720 --> 00:37:35.489
(INAUDIBLE)

833
00:37:35.556 --> 00:37:36.824
This wine is drinking great.

834
00:37:36.891 --> 00:37:38.593
And this food
is eating great.

835
00:37:38.659 --> 00:37:41.428
Be careful. You gonna
give me gout tonight.

836
00:37:41.495 --> 00:37:43.664
It has been such a pleasure
serving you guys.

837
00:37:43.731 --> 00:37:45.499
Uh, dinner's on us tonight.

838
00:37:45.566 --> 00:37:46.601
-What?
-No.

839
00:37:46.667 --> 00:37:48.636
-What? What?
-Yes.

840
00:37:52.907 --> 00:37:53.941
Oh, no.

841
00:37:55.209 --> 00:37:57.211
Fascinating couple
of days, I imagine.

842
00:37:57.277 --> 00:37:59.446
Hey, what's up?
You need something?

843
00:37:59.514 --> 00:38:01.549
I'm kinda busy
ordering clothes.

844
00:38:01.616 --> 00:38:03.518
So, what are you thinking?

845
00:38:03.584 --> 00:38:05.586
The week is over,
are you ready to go back?

846
00:38:06.419 --> 00:38:08.022
Go back?
What do you mean?

847
00:38:08.089 --> 00:38:11.826
Don't you see what's special
about your life as it was?

848
00:38:11.893 --> 00:38:16.597
You see how superficial
a life of wealth and success
ultimately is?

849
00:38:17.364 --> 00:38:18.666
No.

850
00:38:18.733 --> 00:38:23.237
But have you really reflected
on your experience?

851
00:38:23.303 --> 00:38:25.338
Are you nuts?
I was living in my car!

852
00:38:25.405 --> 00:38:27.175
Now I'm living
in this giant house.

853
00:38:27.241 --> 00:38:29.177
I can buy whatever I want,
do whatever I want.

854
00:38:29.243 --> 00:38:31.012
But what about your job?
What about Elena?

855
00:38:31.078 --> 00:38:32.180
What about the pool heater?

856
00:38:32.246 --> 00:38:34.549
Who gives a fuck
about the pool heater?

857
00:38:34.615 --> 00:38:37.652
I show you something
to make you realize
your life is precious.

858
00:38:37.718 --> 00:38:40.420
You see it and you go back.
You can't just stay.

859
00:38:40.487 --> 00:38:43.456
So it's all over?
You're gonna make me go back?

860
00:38:44.258 --> 00:38:45.425
No, I can't do that.

861
00:38:46.459 --> 00:38:48.262
So if I want to stay,
I can just stay?

862
00:38:48.328 --> 00:38:49.764
-Yes.
-I have to want to go back?

863
00:38:49.831 --> 00:38:51.199
-That's right.
-Then I don't want to go back.

864
00:38:51.265 --> 00:38:52.432
But you can't do that!

865
00:38:52.499 --> 00:38:55.102
-You just said I could.
-(GRUMBLES) Shucks.

866
00:38:55.169 --> 00:38:56.771
You guided someone?

867
00:38:56.838 --> 00:39:01.441
Gabriel, you're not
supposed to talk to people
or be visible.

868
00:39:01.509 --> 00:39:04.278
-I know that.
-Then why did you do this?

869
00:39:04.344 --> 00:39:05.880
He was a lost soul.

870
00:39:05.947 --> 00:39:07.114
I tried to show him

871
00:39:07.181 --> 00:39:09.684
that wealth wouldn't
solve all his problems.

872
00:39:09.750 --> 00:39:10.952
And?

873
00:39:11.018 --> 00:39:14.522
It seems to have solved
most of his problems.

874
00:39:14.589 --> 00:39:17.692
Gabriel, you were
supposed to help Elena.

875
00:39:17.758 --> 00:39:20.427
What you've done has
really changed things.

876
00:39:20.493 --> 00:39:22.429
She had to cancel
her date with Arj

877
00:39:22.495 --> 00:39:24.298
and that set off
a chain reaction.

878
00:39:24.364 --> 00:39:26.934
The date went differently,
Arj lost his job,

879
00:39:27.001 --> 00:39:28.401
and that's
what's led us here.

880
00:39:28.468 --> 00:39:30.905
You have to get Arj
to go back.

881
00:39:30.972 --> 00:39:34.575
And until you do,
I have to take your wings.

882
00:39:34.642 --> 00:39:36.476
Oh, man.

883
00:39:36.544 --> 00:39:38.478
Turn around.

884
00:39:42.650 --> 00:39:43.985
(MARTHA SIGHS)

885
00:39:45.987 --> 00:39:48.122
<i>(PUSH IT</i>
BY SALT-N-PEPA PLAYING)

886
00:39:48.189 --> 00:39:49.757
<i>♪ Ow! Baby! ♪</i>

887
00:39:49.824 --> 00:39:51.259
My guy!

888
00:39:52.226 --> 00:39:55.897
Hey! Who wants
some fresh bubble?

889
00:39:56.564 --> 00:39:58.633
Whoa!

890
00:39:58.699 --> 00:40:01.669
Justin needs them bubs.

891
00:40:01.736 --> 00:40:04.772
Elena needs some bubs.

892
00:40:04.839 --> 00:40:06.473
Tell me what you think.
Be honest.

893
00:40:06.540 --> 00:40:08.509
Don't lie to me,
don't lie to me.

894
00:40:09.409 --> 00:40:11.012
How's it drinking?

895
00:40:11.078 --> 00:40:12.947
-That's drinking nice.
-Yes.

896
00:40:14.382 --> 00:40:15.983
Jeff! Come here, man.

897
00:40:16.050 --> 00:40:18.085
Have some wine.
Have a little glass.

898
00:40:18.152 --> 00:40:20.588
-Oh, wow. Thanks.
-Here, have some. Have fun.

899
00:40:23.090 --> 00:40:25.425
-That's really good.
-Yeah.

900
00:40:25.492 --> 00:40:26.961
I should get back
to cleaning up, though.

901
00:40:27.028 --> 00:40:28.930
Good call.
Keep cleaning, Jeff.

902
00:40:29.664 --> 00:40:31.198
Hey!

903
00:40:31.265 --> 00:40:33.200
It's Gabriel!

904
00:40:33.267 --> 00:40:35.202
Gabriel, the angel.

905
00:40:35.269 --> 00:40:37.338
-Where's your little wings?
-I lost them.

906
00:40:37.405 --> 00:40:38.706
Ooh. You've been a bad boy.

907
00:40:38.773 --> 00:40:40.508
So no wings,
what does that mean?

908
00:40:40.574 --> 00:40:42.376
People can see me,
I have less powers.

909
00:40:42.442 --> 00:40:44.512
-It's very embarrassing.
-Uh-oh.

910
00:40:44.578 --> 00:40:47.480
Listen, I know
you like this life,

911
00:40:47.548 --> 00:40:49.482
but may I pose a question?

912
00:40:49.550 --> 00:40:51.185
Is this fair to Jeff?

913
00:40:51.252 --> 00:40:53.354
Jeff? Jeff's chilling.

914
00:40:53.421 --> 00:40:54.555
Is he?

915
00:40:56.257 --> 00:40:57.258
ARJ: What are you doing?

916
00:41:05.299 --> 00:41:07.735
Why am I holding
my own trash?

917
00:41:08.936 --> 00:41:10.071
Why are you in my clothes?

918
00:41:11.806 --> 00:41:13.140
What's happening right now?

919
00:41:13.207 --> 00:41:14.675
What did you do to me?

920
00:41:15.609 --> 00:41:17.645
(HYPERVENTILATING)

921
00:41:19.547 --> 00:41:21.215
-Oh, no.
-What happened?

922
00:41:21.282 --> 00:41:22.482
I gave him his memory back,

923
00:41:22.550 --> 00:41:24.051
but I think he may
have went into shock.

924
00:41:24.118 --> 00:41:25.186
Is he dead?

925
00:41:25.252 --> 00:41:27.154
No. Definitely not.

926
00:41:27.221 --> 00:41:29.724
Oh, shit,
some dude just died.

927
00:41:29.790 --> 00:41:30.992
Let's bounce.

928
00:41:31.058 --> 00:41:32.593
He's not dead!

929
00:41:33.627 --> 00:41:36.263
I hope not.

930
00:41:36.330 --> 00:41:40.034
I did not know you were
struggling to the point
that you needed

931
00:41:40.935 --> 00:41:43.070
divine intervention.

932
00:41:43.137 --> 00:41:44.739
But you got
to switch back, man!

933
00:41:44.805 --> 00:41:46.741
Give me my life back.

934
00:41:46.807 --> 00:41:48.909
So, what? I just go back
to living in my car?

935
00:41:48.976 --> 00:41:51.412
-You lived in your car?
-Yes, Jeff, I did.

936
00:41:51.479 --> 00:41:53.047
Why do you think
an angel got involved?

937
00:41:53.114 --> 00:41:54.415
'Cause I had
too many roommates?

938
00:41:54.482 --> 00:41:56.350
Okay, that's bad.

939
00:41:56.417 --> 00:41:58.019
And I acknowledge that.

940
00:41:58.085 --> 00:41:59.920
So here's
what I'm going to do.

941
00:41:59.987 --> 00:42:01.722
If you switch back
right now,

942
00:42:01.789 --> 00:42:04.859
I'm going
to give you $200,000.

943
00:42:04.925 --> 00:42:07.128
(SNICKERS) You spend more than
that on one of your watches!

944
00:42:07.194 --> 00:42:08.396
You're lowballing me
on your existence?

945
00:42:08.462 --> 00:42:09.463
You live in your car!

946
00:42:09.530 --> 00:42:10.598
I thought that'd be
a lot to you.

947
00:42:10.664 --> 00:42:12.133
-I don't know.
-How greedy are you, man?

948
00:42:12.199 --> 00:42:13.768
I'm not greedy!
It's an opening offer!

949
00:42:13.834 --> 00:42:15.302
-That's how negotiations work.
-That's worth your entire life?

950
00:42:15.369 --> 00:42:16.937
Counter! Make me an offer.

951
00:42:17.004 --> 00:42:18.873
Time out, guys.

952
00:42:18.939 --> 00:42:21.042
You can't do that, Jeff.

953
00:42:21.108 --> 00:42:22.610
This is Arj's experience.

954
00:42:22.676 --> 00:42:25.279
-You might not
remember anything.
-What?

955
00:42:25.346 --> 00:42:26.781
Okay, how's this?

956
00:42:26.847 --> 00:42:29.583
Switch back,
or you are evil,

957
00:42:29.650 --> 00:42:32.386
and this angel man will
send you to Hell forever.

958
00:42:32.453 --> 00:42:33.487
Smite him!

959
00:42:33.554 --> 00:42:35.122
I can't send someone to Hell.

960
00:42:35.189 --> 00:42:36.490
That's actually
not my department.

961
00:42:36.557 --> 00:42:39.393
Good God, man,
you are very unhelpful!

962
00:42:41.228 --> 00:42:42.263
Listen.

963
00:42:43.164 --> 00:42:45.166
I drive around L.A.

964
00:42:45.232 --> 00:42:49.603
I see the homeless,
houseless crisis

965
00:42:49.670 --> 00:42:50.905
that has befallen us,

966
00:42:50.971 --> 00:42:52.973
and I did not know that
you were a part of that,

967
00:42:53.040 --> 00:42:54.275
and I don't want you to be.

968
00:42:54.341 --> 00:42:55.843
But that being said,

