1215
00:53:28.308 --> 00:53:29.911
It's like nothing
I've experienced.

1216
00:53:29.977 --> 00:53:32.080
(CHUCKLING) Yeah, man.

1217
00:53:32.146 --> 00:53:34.649
No? Have a chicken nuggie.

1218
00:53:42.690 --> 00:53:44.792
There you go!
It happened, see?

1219
00:53:44.859 --> 00:53:46.460
Instinct kicked in.

1220
00:53:46.527 --> 00:53:48.596
-Oh. (CHUCKLES)
-Yeah!

1221
00:53:49.797 --> 00:53:52.399
-I like this even more.
-Yeah.

1222
00:53:52.466 --> 00:53:54.168
-Have some milkshake.
-Mmm.

1223
00:54:01.743 --> 00:54:04.645
-Wow.
-(CHUCKLES)

1224
00:54:04.712 --> 00:54:08.783
Jeff, could you imagine
seeing strawberries
for thousands of years

1225
00:54:08.850 --> 00:54:13.353
but never actually knowing
the sweet taste enclosed
in those magical berries?

1226
00:54:14.055 --> 00:54:15.355
I can't imagine.

1227
00:54:15.422 --> 00:54:17.525
And in all fairness,
that's a chocolate milkshake.

1228
00:54:19.560 --> 00:54:22.329
What are we going to do, Jeff?
I'm scared.

1229
00:54:22.395 --> 00:54:23.430
We don't have any money,

1230
00:54:23.497 --> 00:54:25.833
and I'm already
perspiring a lot.

1231
00:54:25.900 --> 00:54:29.302
So I looked up online
how long the average coma lasts.

1232
00:54:29.369 --> 00:54:32.206
Two weeks.
Not that bad, you know.

1233
00:54:32.272 --> 00:54:34.942
So we just got to make
enough money to last
until this guy wakes up.

1234
00:54:35.009 --> 00:54:36.978
Tomorrow, I'll go
to my old office.

1235
00:54:37.044 --> 00:54:39.647
I know everything
about all the companies
they've invested in.

1236
00:54:39.714 --> 00:54:41.281
So, I'll give them
some insight

1237
00:54:41.348 --> 00:54:43.383
that makes me look
like a financial genius.

1238
00:54:43.450 --> 00:54:44.719
They'll hire me on the spot.

1239
00:54:44.786 --> 00:54:46.521
It'll be enough money
for both of us.

1240
00:54:46.587 --> 00:54:48.990
We'll be out
of that motel tomorrow.

1241
00:54:52.794 --> 00:54:53.795
There you go.

1242
00:54:54.361 --> 00:54:55.495
There you go!

1243
00:54:55.563 --> 00:54:57.497
You're a big boy, huh?

1244
00:54:57.565 --> 00:54:59.534
-Yeah, I'm a big boy.
-(CHUCKLES)

1245
00:54:59.600 --> 00:55:00.802
You sure are.

1246
00:55:02.302 --> 00:55:04.906
Let go of me!
Let go of me!

1247
00:55:07.074 --> 00:55:08.976
Did you get the job?

1248
00:55:09.043 --> 00:55:11.012
Does it look like
I got the job?

1249
00:55:11.078 --> 00:55:12.246
No!

1250
00:55:12.312 --> 00:55:14.048
They accused me
of hacking into their files,

1251
00:55:14.115 --> 00:55:16.751
and then they basically
threatened to kill me.

1252
00:55:16.818 --> 00:55:18.418
-Oh, no.
-Yeah.

1253
00:55:19.419 --> 00:55:21.354
Chicken nuggie?

1254
00:55:21.421 --> 00:55:25.993
Yes, of course I respect
patient confidentiality.

1255
00:55:26.060 --> 00:55:27.528
I just need to know,

1256
00:55:27.595 --> 00:55:31.232
do you have
any Indian dudes there
that are in a coma?

1257
00:55:31.299 --> 00:55:33.568
Yes, I've actually
called many times.

1258
00:55:33.634 --> 00:55:35.502
Hello? Hello?

1259
00:55:37.672 --> 00:55:38.940
I don't think
they're going to tell me

1260
00:55:39.006 --> 00:55:41.008
any more information
about this.

1261
00:55:41.909 --> 00:55:43.110
It's been three weeks,

1262
00:55:43.177 --> 00:55:45.546
I've applied
for one million jobs.

1263
00:55:45.613 --> 00:55:47.114
I either
don't hear back at all

1264
00:55:47.181 --> 00:55:48.448
or it's a scam
where people just want me

1265
00:55:48.516 --> 00:55:50.785
to send them pictures
of my feet.

1266
00:55:50.852 --> 00:55:52.653
Are you listening
to me, Gabriel?

1267
00:55:53.921 --> 00:55:56.691
Sorry. The Internet
is amazing, Jeff.

1268
00:55:56.757 --> 00:55:58.559
I want
to help you find jobs,

1269
00:55:58.626 --> 00:56:01.461
but I also want to look
at photos of baby elephants.

1270
00:56:01.529 --> 00:56:02.597
(CHUCKLES)

1271
00:56:02.663 --> 00:56:05.199
Look at this guy,
bathing in a river.

1272
00:56:05.266 --> 00:56:06.601
His name's Oliver.

1273
00:56:06.667 --> 00:56:09.270
I cannot financially support
the both of us anymore.

1274
00:56:09.337 --> 00:56:10.972
You have to get
a job, Gabriel.

1275
00:56:11.038 --> 00:56:12.607
-A job?
-Yeah.

1276
00:56:12.673 --> 00:56:15.743
Wow.
Wonder what I want to be.

1277
00:56:15.810 --> 00:56:18.045
An architect, a scientist.

1278
00:56:18.112 --> 00:56:19.513
Maybe I want
to work with animals.

1279
00:56:20.114 --> 00:56:21.148
Oh.

1280
00:56:21.215 --> 00:56:23.217
Maybe I could work
with baby elephants.

1281
00:56:24.018 --> 00:56:25.019
Maybe.

1282
00:56:26.287 --> 00:56:27.454
But probably not.

1283
00:56:27.521 --> 00:56:28.556
FELIPE: Come on, Gabriel.

1284
00:56:28.623 --> 00:56:30.258
You need to move
more fast, please.

1285
00:56:31.859 --> 00:56:32.894
Do we do any other stuff

1286
00:56:32.960 --> 00:56:34.427
or is it just dishes
all night?

1287
00:56:34.494 --> 00:56:36.264
Just washing
dishes all night.

1288
00:56:40.234 --> 00:56:42.136
My first check.

1289
00:56:42.203 --> 00:56:44.471
Felipe, my first check.

1290
00:56:44.538 --> 00:56:45.539
Good, Gabe.

1291
00:56:47.375 --> 00:56:49.010
You're shitting me.

1292
00:56:49.076 --> 00:56:51.979
Felipe, there's something
wrong with my check!

1293
00:56:52.046 --> 00:56:54.481
FELIPE: What's wrong
with your check, Gabe?

1294
00:56:54.548 --> 00:56:57.585
There's not enough money.
Where's the money?

1295
00:56:57.652 --> 00:56:59.186
They're paying one number,

1296
00:56:59.253 --> 00:57:02.290
and then taking a lot of money
for all these other things.

1297
00:57:02.356 --> 00:57:03.591
Let me see, Gabe.

1298
00:57:05.293 --> 00:57:08.262
This money goes
to the local government,
federal government,

1299
00:57:08.329 --> 00:57:09.964
your insurance,
and your social security.

1300
00:57:10.031 --> 00:57:11.065
That's why it's less money.

1301
00:57:12.900 --> 00:57:15.136
I can't make enough money
to live off this.

1302
00:57:15.202 --> 00:57:17.038
FELIPE: You may need
to get another job.

1303
00:57:17.104 --> 00:57:18.506
Another job?

1304
00:57:18.572 --> 00:57:21.642
I wash dishes all the time.
When can I do another job?

1305
00:57:21.709 --> 00:57:23.476
FELIPE: I don't know.
I have three jobs.

1306
00:57:26.414 --> 00:57:28.182
-What?
-I work here,

1307
00:57:28.249 --> 00:57:29.850
I'm a mechanic,

1308
00:57:29.917 --> 00:57:33.220
and I do valet parking
at an escape room.

1309
00:57:33.287 --> 00:57:36.557
I thought a job gives me
enough money for all my things

1310
00:57:36.624 --> 00:57:40.161
and some extra money
to spend on fun stuff.

1311
00:57:40.227 --> 00:57:42.763
Sorry, Gabe.
This is how it is.

1312
00:57:53.607 --> 00:57:55.910
-How you feeling?
-I'm good.

1313
00:57:55.977 --> 00:57:59.146
It's a big day tomorrow.
Are you excited?

1314
00:57:59.213 --> 00:58:03.150
-Yeah. Ready to go home.
-That's good.

1315
00:58:03.217 --> 00:58:04.919
So, listen.

1316
00:58:04.986 --> 00:58:06.854
Since you've been here,
there have been two guys

1317
00:58:06.921 --> 00:58:08.823
who've been
asking around about you,

1318
00:58:08.889 --> 00:58:10.691
seemed a little bit shady.

1319
00:58:10.758 --> 00:58:13.594
One, curly hair,
pretty bland.

1320
00:58:13.661 --> 00:58:15.529
The other guy, long hair,

1321
00:58:15.596 --> 00:58:17.565
very attractive.

1322
00:58:17.631 --> 00:58:19.700
He's kinda like a bad boy,
but with a soft touch.

1323
00:58:19.767 --> 00:58:21.235
I know who you're
talking about.

1324
00:58:21.302 --> 00:58:23.704
-Yes, I know them.
-Maybe give them a call.

1325
00:58:23.771 --> 00:58:25.439
They seemed
pretty concerned.

1326
00:58:25.506 --> 00:58:27.441
You could give
the tall one my number.

1327
00:58:27.508 --> 00:58:28.776
That's fine with me.

1328
00:58:31.245 --> 00:58:33.047
Can I ask you something?

1329
00:58:33.114 --> 00:58:35.049
When people have
accidents like this, do...

1330
00:58:35.116 --> 00:58:36.951
Do they ever have
memory issues?

1331
00:58:41.489 --> 00:58:43.424
(ROBOT BEEPS)

1332
00:58:43.491 --> 00:58:44.892
JEFF: Where is this place?

1333
00:58:46.694 --> 00:58:48.929
"Stone Canyon Road"?

1334
00:58:48.996 --> 00:58:50.564
That's my address.

1335
00:58:51.866 --> 00:58:53.734
"Delivery for Arj"?

1336
00:58:54.535 --> 00:58:56.470
He's out of the coma.

1337
00:58:56.537 --> 00:58:58.172
He's out of the coma!

1338
00:59:00.307 --> 00:59:03.911
(DOORBELL RINGING)

1339
00:59:03.978 --> 00:59:05.212
ARJ: Jeff?

1340
00:59:05.279 --> 00:59:06.881
The fuck is he doing here?

1341
00:59:06.947 --> 00:59:07.915
(PHONE CHIMES)

1342
00:59:08.983 --> 00:59:10.918
He's my Foodzr driver?

1343
00:59:17.892 --> 00:59:19.060
Hey, thanks so much.

1344
00:59:19.994 --> 00:59:21.262
What is
happening right now?

1345
00:59:21.328 --> 00:59:23.631
You're out of the coma
and you're ordering ramen?

1346
00:59:23.697 --> 00:59:25.166
Why didn't you
phone me, Arj?

1347
00:59:25.232 --> 00:59:27.968
(SIGHS) They said
this might happen.

1348
00:59:28.035 --> 00:59:30.638
Because of the coma,
I've been having
some memory issues.

1349
00:59:30.704 --> 00:59:32.840
I'm so sorry,
but I don't remember you.

1350
00:59:33.542 --> 00:59:35.510
You don't remember me?

1351
00:59:35.576 --> 00:59:37.678
The pamphlet.
Let me get you a pamphlet.

1352
00:59:44.085 --> 00:59:45.119
Here you go.

1353
00:59:45.186 --> 00:59:47.488
It's called
dissociative memory loss.

1354
00:59:47.556 --> 00:59:51.526
It's due to the medications
they were using to treat me
after the accident.

1355
00:59:51.592 --> 00:59:54.161
It was pretty serious
brain trauma.

1356
00:59:54.228 --> 00:59:55.296
Are you
fucking with me, man?

1357
00:59:55.362 --> 00:59:56.630
Do you actually
not remember me?

1358
00:59:56.697 --> 00:59:58.499
Maybe we can try
to jog my memory.

1359
00:59:58.567 --> 01:00:00.267
-What's your name?
-Jeff!

1360
01:00:00.334 --> 01:00:04.038
Uh, that's not
ringing a bell.

1361
01:00:04.105 --> 01:00:05.439
You don't know who I am?

1362
01:00:05.507 --> 01:00:07.942
If you read the pamphlet,
it could be very helpful.

1363
01:00:08.008 --> 01:00:09.677
JEFF: "The duration
of memory loss can vary

1364
01:00:09.743 --> 01:00:12.446
"depending on the specific
cause of the coma.

1365
01:00:12.514 --> 01:00:15.616
"In some cases,
memory may improve
over time with treatment.

1366
01:00:15.683 --> 01:00:17.586
"In other cases,
memory loss...

1367
01:00:18.886 --> 01:00:20.221
"may be permanent."

1368
01:00:20.888 --> 01:00:22.289
Wow.

1369
01:00:22.356 --> 01:00:23.592
That's <i>no bueno.</i>

1370
01:00:25.527 --> 01:00:27.661
Did you just say,
"That's <i>no bueno"?</i>

1371
01:00:28.829 --> 01:00:31.398
No fucking shit,
it's <i>no bueno!</i>

1372
01:00:31.465 --> 01:00:35.402
It's <i>muy, muy,</i>
<i>muy no bueno,</i> Gabriel.

1373
01:00:35.469 --> 01:00:37.738
You know what?
I want to talk to God.

1374
01:00:37.805 --> 01:00:39.907
Get me God.
I want a meeting
with God right now.

1375
01:00:39.974 --> 01:00:41.242
That's above
my pay grade.

1376
01:00:41.308 --> 01:00:42.743
Well, then who's your boss?
Who do you work for?

1377
01:00:42.810 --> 01:00:44.145
Martha.

1378
01:00:44.211 --> 01:00:45.547
Martha?

1379
01:00:45.614 --> 01:00:47.882
You work for an angel
named Martha?

1380
01:00:47.948 --> 01:00:49.150
Martha.

1381
01:00:50.284 --> 01:00:51.652
What has happened
to you, Gabriel?

1382
01:00:51.719 --> 01:00:52.920
You've just given up.

1383
01:00:52.987 --> 01:00:54.321
You're smoking
cigarettes now?

1384
01:00:54.388 --> 01:00:57.925
Leave me alone, Jeff.
I like it. It's all I have.

1385
01:00:59.760 --> 01:01:01.228
Please don't
give up on me.

1386
01:01:01.295 --> 01:01:03.898
Do you want to wash dishes
and smoke cigarettes

1387
01:01:03.964 --> 01:01:05.432
or do you want
to get your wings back?

1388
01:01:05.499 --> 01:01:08.637
You can get them back, man.
I know you can. Just think!

1389
01:01:13.807 --> 01:01:15.676
His friend Elena.

1390
01:01:15.743 --> 01:01:17.512
She was the one I was
supposed to help originally,

1391
01:01:17.579 --> 01:01:20.515
but I didn't,
and she went off her path.

1392
01:01:20.582 --> 01:01:23.552
Maybe I can help her
get back on her path

1393
01:01:23.618 --> 01:01:26.220
and that'll help Arj
get back on his path.

1394
01:01:26.287 --> 01:01:27.888
And then he'll want
to switch back.

1395
01:01:27.955 --> 01:01:30.257
And then I'll get
my wings back.

1396
01:01:30.324 --> 01:01:32.493
And then you'll get
your life back!

1397
01:01:32.561 --> 01:01:34.795
That's what I want.
I knew you could do it, man!

1398
01:01:34.862 --> 01:01:36.197
Good job. You can
do this, Gabriel.

1399
01:01:36.263 --> 01:01:37.431
-Yes, yes.
-FELIPE: Hey, Gabriel,

1400
01:01:37.498 --> 01:01:38.899
what are you doing there?
Your break is over.

1401
01:01:38.966 --> 01:01:40.434
I need you, please.

1402
01:01:40.501 --> 01:01:43.370
-You need to come back
to the restaurant.
-Okay, Felipe.

1403
01:01:43.437 --> 01:01:44.905
I got to finish
my shift first.

1404
01:01:47.374 --> 01:01:49.043
Thanks, man.

1405
01:02:00.888 --> 01:02:04.391
That right there,
that's the truth.

1406
01:02:04.458 --> 01:02:06.293
I had a union
at my last job,

1407
01:02:06.360 --> 01:02:07.828
all they did was take money
out our checks,

1408
01:02:07.895 --> 01:02:10.064
ain't do nothing for us.

1409
01:02:10.130 --> 01:02:12.634
But, Kirby,
how could you say that
when that's not even us?

1410
01:02:12.701 --> 01:02:14.902
Sounds like
the same nonsense to me.

1411
01:02:14.969 --> 01:02:17.471
If that's not the truth,
what is?

1412
01:02:17.539 --> 01:02:19.907
The truth is that one
of our team members

1413
01:02:19.974 --> 01:02:22.611
had a panic attack
on the floor last week,

1414
01:02:22.677 --> 01:02:24.144
picking and choosing
which bills to pay,

1415
01:02:24.211 --> 01:02:25.813
worried about
getting evicted.

1416
01:02:25.879 --> 01:02:27.549
And I know
she's not the only one
that has to deal with this.

1417
01:02:28.550 --> 01:02:29.850
I mean, guys,
they're giving us

1418
01:02:29.917 --> 01:02:31.986
more and more
double shifts,

1419
01:02:32.052 --> 01:02:34.455
less training,
more responsibilities.

1420
01:02:34.522 --> 01:02:35.789
And what do we get for it?

1421
01:02:35.856 --> 01:02:38.627
Twenty-five cents a raise
and a pat on the back?

1422
01:02:38.693 --> 01:02:42.329
It is very possible for this
place to take care of itself
and the people in it,

1423
01:02:42.396 --> 01:02:43.764
but they keep giving us
less and less

1424
01:02:43.831 --> 01:02:46.601
because we're okay
taking crumbs.

1425
01:02:46.668 --> 01:02:48.302
So what's it going to be?

1426
01:02:48.369 --> 01:02:50.538
Are we going
to take the crumbs?

1427
01:02:50.605 --> 01:02:53.440
Or are we going
to fuck 'em up?

1428
01:02:53.508 --> 01:02:54.808
(ALL APPLAUDING)

1429
01:02:55.943 --> 01:02:56.944
GABRIEL: Yeah!

1430
01:02:58.379 --> 01:03:00.615
And you know what else?

1431
01:03:00.682 --> 01:03:04.719
Why do we need to give money
to taxes and social security?

1432
01:03:05.919 --> 01:03:09.023
That money needs
to go to fun stuff,

1433
01:03:09.089 --> 01:03:11.760
like chicken nuggies
and milkshakes.

1434
01:03:13.093 --> 01:03:15.963
Milkshakes are good,
chicken nuggies are good.

1435
01:03:16.030 --> 01:03:17.898
That's the truth.

1436
01:03:17.965 --> 01:03:19.300
And dogs.

1437
01:03:19.366 --> 01:03:21.468
I petted a dog
for the first time
the other day.

1438
01:03:21.536 --> 01:03:24.138
Maybe they need
to get benefits, too.

1439
01:03:24.204 --> 01:03:26.340
They give so much joy,
and what do they get?

1440
01:03:26.407 --> 01:03:28.475
A pat on the head
and a biscuit.

1441
01:03:29.443 --> 01:03:31.145
It's not enough!

1442
01:03:31.211 --> 01:03:33.314
We can do better.

1443
01:03:33.380 --> 01:03:36.350
And Hardware Heaven
can do better.

1444
01:03:36.417 --> 01:03:40.187
For us
and for the dogs.

1445
01:03:40.254 --> 01:03:42.657
ELENA: (CHUCKLES)
Hey, brother.

1446
01:03:42.724 --> 01:03:44.693
What department
you work in?

1447
01:03:44.759 --> 01:03:47.027
GABRIEL:
Oh, I don't work here.

1448
01:03:47.094 --> 01:03:48.395
I'm a dishwasher

1449
01:03:48.462 --> 01:03:50.097
at an all-you-can-eat
Korean barbecue restaurant.

1450
01:03:51.666 --> 01:03:53.500
Am I not supposed
to be here?

1451
01:04:05.580 --> 01:04:06.681
WOMAN: Yes.

1452
01:04:08.115 --> 01:04:09.116
No.

1453
01:04:10.851 --> 01:04:12.119
No.

1454
01:04:13.153 --> 01:04:14.288
No.

1455
01:04:15.255 --> 01:04:16.290
No.

1456
01:04:17.358 --> 01:04:18.392
No.

1457
01:04:19.026 --> 01:04:20.060
No.

1458
01:04:43.718 --> 01:04:44.918
You're okay, Gabe?

1459
01:04:46.688 --> 01:04:48.055
