And it's beautiful.

1703
01:15:59.360 --> 01:16:01.762
Damn! I want to go.

1704
01:16:01.829 --> 01:16:03.764
I want to go
to Paris, but...

1705
01:16:05.366 --> 01:16:06.367
(SIGHS)

1706
01:16:08.135 --> 01:16:11.372
I know what's going on
on the ground down there.

1707
01:16:14.208 --> 01:16:16.143
And instead
of being up here

1708
01:16:16.210 --> 01:16:17.912
drinking the fanciest
wine you got,

1709
01:16:17.978 --> 01:16:20.081
I guess I'd rather
be down there...

1710
01:16:22.183 --> 01:16:24.285
fighting to get
more people up here,

1711
01:16:25.386 --> 01:16:27.021
rather than just myself.

1712
01:16:33.227 --> 01:16:34.628
(SIGHING) I got to go.

1713
01:17:48.903 --> 01:17:50.271
Pretty Baby.

1714
01:17:53.440 --> 01:17:55.276
(ZIPPING UP BAG)

1715
01:17:59.113 --> 01:18:02.016
(ARJ SCREAMING)

1716
01:18:02.082 --> 01:18:04.218
(GROANS) You shot me!

1717
01:18:04.285 --> 01:18:07.556
-(JEFF SCREAMING)
-Oh, no, Jeff! Are you okay?

1718
01:18:07.622 --> 01:18:09.056
(SCREAMING)
Why'd you shoot me?

1719
01:18:09.123 --> 01:18:11.125
You said, "Don't hesitate.
Shoot first, questions later."

1720
01:18:11.192 --> 01:18:13.727
I thought you were
a home invader on meth!

1721
01:18:14.695 --> 01:18:15.829
I said that?

1722
01:18:16.631 --> 01:18:18.199
You remember me?

1723
01:18:18.265 --> 01:18:21.068
When I brought you
that ramen and gyoza,
you remembered me!

1724
01:18:21.135 --> 01:18:22.703
-I knew it!
-(SCREAMS) I'm so sorry!

1725
01:18:22.770 --> 01:18:23.904
I'm going to call 911!

1726
01:18:23.971 --> 01:18:25.206
-I'm doing that now!
-You fucking asshole.

1727
01:18:25.272 --> 01:18:27.741
I knew it! You lied to me
and you shot me!

1728
01:18:27.808 --> 01:18:29.109
You're a bad man, Arj!

1729
01:18:29.176 --> 01:18:31.779
(GRUNTS IN FRUSTRATION)
I can't find my phone!

1730
01:18:31.845 --> 01:18:32.947
JEFF: Use mine!

1731
01:18:33.013 --> 01:18:35.382
(SCREAMS)

1732
01:18:35.449 --> 01:18:36.717
-Arj?
-(JEFF SCREAMS)

1733
01:18:36.784 --> 01:18:37.985
Jeff, are you okay?

1734
01:18:38.052 --> 01:18:40.287
Gabriel, call an angel
that deals with gunshots!

1735
01:18:40.354 --> 01:18:41.656
I have no way
to contact them,

1736
01:18:41.722 --> 01:18:43.592
and they usually work
in a different part of town.

1737
01:18:43.658 --> 01:18:44.925
JEFF: I brought you
into my life,

1738
01:18:44.992 --> 01:18:47.261
I gave you burrata,

1739
01:18:47.328 --> 01:18:49.430
and then you took
everything from me.

1740
01:18:51.865 --> 01:18:56.804
You lied to me,
you stole all my dance moves,

1741
01:18:56.870 --> 01:18:58.205
and then you shot me.

1742
01:19:00.374 --> 01:19:02.910
I'm sorry, man.
Why'd you have a gun
in the first place?

1743
01:19:02.977 --> 01:19:05.312
Well, I didn't think I'd be
the one who'd get shot by it.

1744
01:19:05.379 --> 01:19:06.914
Statistically,
you'd be surprised.

1745
01:19:06.981 --> 01:19:09.883
Okay, not now.
Is that all right?

1746
01:19:10.918 --> 01:19:12.419
Why did you lie to me, Arj?

1747
01:19:14.221 --> 01:19:16.156
My life is hard.

1748
01:19:16.223 --> 01:19:18.792
Yours is
really easy and fun.

1749
01:19:18.859 --> 01:19:19.893
I couldn't go back.

1750
01:19:20.995 --> 01:19:24.765
But it's gone on
long enough.

1751
01:19:24.832 --> 01:19:27.702
Gabriel,
how do I switch back?

1752
01:19:28.902 --> 01:19:30.271
Well, you've told me.

1753
01:19:31.405 --> 01:19:32.473
If you want
to switch back

1754
01:19:32.540 --> 01:19:33.742
to your old life,
it should happen.

1755
01:19:34.609 --> 01:19:36.143
Well, why isn't it happening?

1756
01:19:36.210 --> 01:19:39.681
You want to go back
because you feel guilty
about Jeff,

1757
01:19:39.748 --> 01:19:44.251
but you still don't feel
your life, your real life,
is worth living.

1758
01:19:44.952 --> 01:19:47.221
You don't have hope.

1759
01:19:47.288 --> 01:19:50.224
Just to be clear, he does not
only have to want to go back,

1760
01:19:50.291 --> 01:19:52.893
which was what I thought
we've been going for
this whole time,

1761
01:19:52.960 --> 01:19:54.395
he has to be
psyched about it?

1762
01:19:54.461 --> 01:19:55.796
Yes.

1763
01:19:55.863 --> 01:19:57.464
Well, why would
that ever happen?

1764
01:19:58.198 --> 01:20:00.034
No offense.

1765
01:20:00.100 --> 01:20:02.336
I don't know
what else we can do.

1766
01:20:02.403 --> 01:20:04.905
This has been
a very stressful week.

1767
01:20:04.972 --> 01:20:06.608
Maybe we go back
to my house?

1768
01:20:07.441 --> 01:20:08.677
Technically, your house.

1769
01:20:09.778 --> 01:20:11.278
Our house?

1770
01:20:12.413 --> 01:20:13.581
For now.

1771
01:20:14.582 --> 01:20:15.650
Can I come?

1772
01:20:15.717 --> 01:20:16.917
Yes.

1773
01:20:19.788 --> 01:20:20.854
Like it?

1774
01:20:21.955 --> 01:20:22.956
Yeah.

1775
01:20:23.891 --> 01:20:25.727
I needed this.

1776
01:20:25.794 --> 01:20:29.430
It's the back and forth that
really makes the experience.

1777
01:20:29.496 --> 01:20:30.699
Yeah.

1778
01:20:30.765 --> 01:20:33.067
Shall we plunge?

1779
01:20:33.133 --> 01:20:34.736
What's that?

1780
01:20:34.803 --> 01:20:36.337
Let's go! Let's go!

1781
01:20:36.403 --> 01:20:38.339
(GABRIEL SCREAMS)

1782
01:20:38.405 --> 01:20:39.674
-(TIMER BEEPING)
-You did it, two minutes!

1783
01:20:39.741 --> 01:20:41.842
-You did it, you did it!
-Yeah, Gabriel! Let's go!

1784
01:20:41.909 --> 01:20:43.778
-I'm getting in, too.
-Yep.

1785
01:20:43.844 --> 01:20:45.112
<i>(BOYS (SUMMER TIME LOVE)</i>
BY SABRINA PLAYING)

1786
01:20:45.179 --> 01:20:47.682
Oh, fuck,
I've been shot!

1787
01:20:47.749 --> 01:20:49.651
I shouldn't do this.
I shouldn't do this.

1788
01:20:49.718 --> 01:20:51.553
<i>♪ Boys, boys, boys</i>
<i>Get ready for my love ♪</i>

1789
01:20:51.619 --> 01:20:55.289
-(MIMICS DINOSAUR ROARING)
-(JEFF EXCLAIMING)

1790
01:20:55.356 --> 01:20:57.257
<i>♪ ...in summertime love ♪</i>

1791
01:20:57.324 --> 01:21:00.461
<i>♪ Be my lover, be my baby ♪</i>

1792
01:21:02.096 --> 01:21:04.198
JEFF: You actually learned
to drive the Porsche?

1793
01:21:04.264 --> 01:21:05.633
ARJ: Yeah. I mean,
I know how to drive manual.

1794
01:21:05.700 --> 01:21:06.900
You got to...
You got to learn.
I'll teach you.

1795
01:21:06.967 --> 01:21:09.303
JEFF: I do. Please do.
It looks so fun.

1796
01:21:10.504 --> 01:21:11.905
Have a nice swim?

1797
01:21:13.207 --> 01:21:14.975
Martha.

1798
01:21:15.042 --> 01:21:17.144
Yeah, I guess.

1799
01:21:17.211 --> 01:21:19.046
(MARTHA CHUCKLES)

1800
01:21:19.113 --> 01:21:23.752
So, now Arj wants to go back,
but he still can't.

1801
01:21:23.818 --> 01:21:25.720
Wow.

1802
01:21:25.787 --> 01:21:29.123
I gave you
the easiest assignment.

1803
01:21:29.189 --> 01:21:31.158
All you had to do was
give someone a nudge,

1804
01:21:31.225 --> 01:21:34.261
they look right at the road,
and you were done for the day.

1805
01:21:34.328 --> 01:21:35.663
I know.

1806
01:21:35.730 --> 01:21:37.431
I just thought
I could do more.

1807
01:21:37.498 --> 01:21:39.667
Oh, you certainly
have done more.

1808
01:21:39.734 --> 01:21:42.936
You've been washing dishes,
eating chicken nuggies,

1809
01:21:43.003 --> 01:21:46.340
smoking, drinking,
making speeches.

1810
01:21:46.407 --> 01:21:48.610
Oh, I've seen it all.

1811
01:21:48.676 --> 01:21:51.613
How do I get him to have
hope for his life?

1812
01:21:51.679 --> 01:21:53.180
I lived like he did,

1813
01:21:53.247 --> 01:21:56.250
I understand now why he didn't
have hope in the first place.

1814
01:21:56.316 --> 01:21:57.886
Gabriel...

1815
01:21:59.219 --> 01:22:02.590
sometimes a lost soul
doesn't need an angel.

1816
01:22:02.657 --> 01:22:04.458
It just needs
another person.

1817
01:22:06.226 --> 01:22:08.028
I don't understand.

1818
01:22:09.062 --> 01:22:10.097
I know.

1819
01:22:11.365 --> 01:22:12.399
But I have hope.

1820
01:22:13.568 --> 01:22:14.769
ARJ: Hey, Gabriel!

1821
01:22:16.437 --> 01:22:17.672
You hungry?

1822
01:22:17.739 --> 01:22:20.040
-GABRIEL: Always.
-Let's eat.

1823
01:22:32.052 --> 01:22:34.321
My two favorite things
since I've been a human

1824
01:22:34.388 --> 01:22:37.692
are dancing and tacos.

1825
01:22:37.759 --> 01:22:41.495
-I've been a human way longer,
still two of my favorites.
-JEFF: Mine too.

1826
01:22:41.563 --> 01:22:44.097
-(WOMAN CHUCKLES)
-ARJ: Elena?

1827
01:22:45.365 --> 01:22:47.201
Hey. One second.

1828
01:22:47.267 --> 01:22:49.369
-How's it going?
-ARJ: Uh, I'm good.

1829
01:22:49.436 --> 01:22:52.473
I'm just grabbing some tacos
with some pals. How are you?

1830
01:22:52.540 --> 01:22:54.576
Good. Here with
the Hardware Heaven crew.

1831
01:22:54.642 --> 01:22:56.578
We just had a meeting
and grabbing a bite to eat.

1832
01:22:56.644 --> 01:22:58.178
A meeting?

1833
01:22:58.245 --> 01:23:00.180
We're going
to give it another go
at organizing the store.

1834
01:23:00.247 --> 01:23:01.816
You are?

1835
01:23:01.883 --> 01:23:03.217
Yeah.

1836
01:23:03.283 --> 01:23:05.920
I know I was down about it,
you know, last we talked.

1837
01:23:05.986 --> 01:23:07.087
But I don't know, man,

1838
01:23:07.154 --> 01:23:09.524
I just realized
that change is difficult.

1839
01:23:09.591 --> 01:23:11.659
You're changing something,
you know.

1840
01:23:11.726 --> 01:23:13.227
And no, we won't
win right away,

1841
01:23:13.293 --> 01:23:14.896
but you keep fighting

1842
01:23:14.963 --> 01:23:16.798
and fighting
and fighting, and...

1843
01:23:18.131 --> 01:23:20.434
Because of that,
you eventually do.

1844
01:23:20.501 --> 01:23:21.870
That's what I believe.

1845
01:23:24.772 --> 01:23:26.541
We're going to grab
a drink after this.

1846
01:23:26.608 --> 01:23:28.576
Do you know
any good spots nearby?

1847
01:23:28.643 --> 01:23:29.811
GABRIEL: I know one.

1848
01:23:31.846 --> 01:23:33.313
(CUMBIA MUSIC PLAYING)

1849
01:23:42.356 --> 01:23:43.591
ELENA: Hey!

1850
01:23:43.658 --> 01:23:44.726
I remember
where I know you from.

1851
01:23:44.792 --> 01:23:46.026
You broke into
the break room.

1852
01:23:46.093 --> 01:23:47.662
Uh, milkshake
and chicken nuggies guy.

1853
01:23:47.729 --> 01:23:49.564
-That's you, right?
-Yeah, that's me.

1854
01:23:49.631 --> 01:23:50.632
How's it going?

1855
01:23:51.198 --> 01:23:52.199
Good.

1856
01:23:56.604 --> 01:23:58.706
Whoa. Look at Gabriel go.

1857
01:23:58.773 --> 01:24:02.075
He's got some moves.
He really got into cumbia.

1858
01:24:02.142 --> 01:24:04.478
Everyone learned
to dance except me.

1859
01:24:26.066 --> 01:24:27.067
ARJ: Gabriel.

1860
01:24:28.536 --> 01:24:29.938
What's wrong?

1861
01:24:33.373 --> 01:24:35.108
I'm a failure.

1862
01:24:35.175 --> 01:24:38.913
I've put you and Jeff
in a terrible situation.

1863
01:24:38.980 --> 01:24:40.615
It's all my fault.

1864
01:24:40.682 --> 01:24:44.084
What? None of that's true.
You were just trying to help.

1865
01:24:44.151 --> 01:24:46.353
My boss told me
I wasn't ready,

1866
01:24:46.420 --> 01:24:48.056
and she knew the truth.

1867
01:24:49.156 --> 01:24:50.223
What truth?

1868
01:24:52.192 --> 01:24:53.795
That I'm kind of a dum-dum.

1869
01:24:53.861 --> 01:24:55.930
A dum-dum?
You're not a dum-dum.

1870
01:24:55.997 --> 01:24:57.999
I'm a dum-dum,
and I give up.

1871
01:24:58.066 --> 01:24:59.333
You can't give up.

1872
01:24:59.399 --> 01:25:02.102
-You did.
-(SIGHS)

1873
01:25:02.169 --> 01:25:05.840
But, Gabriel, I lost my job,
I lost my apartment.

1874
01:25:05.907 --> 01:25:07.207
I lost my job.

1875
01:25:07.274 --> 01:25:09.443
I used to be
a celestial being,

1876
01:25:09.510 --> 01:25:11.846
and now I'm a chain-smoker.

1877
01:25:11.913 --> 01:25:14.314
I'm addicted to nicotine.

1878
01:25:14.381 --> 01:25:16.985
Yeah, but it's not over,
is it?

1879
01:25:17.051 --> 01:25:18.820
I mean, you came down
to show me

1880
01:25:18.886 --> 01:25:20.722
that my life's
worth living.

1881
01:25:20.788 --> 01:25:22.122
Come on, let's go.

1882
01:25:22.189 --> 01:25:24.124
I tried, Arj.

1883
01:25:24.191 --> 01:25:25.560
But it seems
you prefer to live

1884
01:25:25.627 --> 01:25:27.695
in a giant mansion
with a pool

1885
01:25:27.762 --> 01:25:31.498
to sleeping in your car
and eating protein bars.

1886
01:25:31.566 --> 01:25:33.735
But, Gabriel, I never
wanted all that stuff.

1887
01:25:33.801 --> 01:25:36.403
I just wanted enough,
enough to be comfortable,

1888
01:25:36.470 --> 01:25:39.807
to not feel like I was
struggling all the time.

1889
01:25:39.874 --> 01:25:44.211
If I go back,
will I have my car,
a job, anything?

1890
01:25:44.277 --> 01:25:47.481
No to all those things.

1891
01:25:47.548 --> 01:25:49.282
Well, that's pretty scary.

1892
01:25:52.587 --> 01:25:55.489
When I got fired,
I was scared, too.

1893
01:25:55.556 --> 01:25:58.191
I didn't know
what was going to happen.

1894
01:25:58.258 --> 01:25:59.794
And a lot of times,
it wasn't fun.

1895
01:26:01.696 --> 01:26:03.998
Sleeping in your car
wasn't fun,

1896
01:26:04.065 --> 01:26:08.603
being hungry wasn't fun,
washing dishes wasn't fun.

1897
01:26:09.137 --> 01:26:10.138
But...

1898
01:26:11.906 --> 01:26:14.742
I love being human.

1899
01:26:14.809 --> 01:26:19.279
I love dancing, I love tacos,
I love Felipe, I love Jeff.

1900
01:26:19.346 --> 01:26:21.015
And I love you.

1901
01:26:24.152 --> 01:26:26.054
If I go back,
what happens to you?

1902
01:26:26.120 --> 01:26:27.689
Will I ever see you again?

1903
01:26:27.755 --> 01:26:29.189
No.

1904
01:26:29.256 --> 01:26:32.060
My job would be done,
I'll be an angel again.

1905
01:26:33.326 --> 01:26:36.229
No more tacos.

1906
01:26:36.296 --> 01:26:38.498
Maybe I'll leave one out
for you, just in case.

1907
01:26:41.969 --> 01:26:43.071
(ARJ CHUCKLES)

1908
01:26:44.172 --> 01:26:45.940
What?

1909
01:26:46.007 --> 01:26:48.810
(SIGHS) One time,
I took my dad for tacos,

1910
01:26:48.876 --> 01:26:50.545
and I got him this shirt
for his birthday,

1911
01:26:50.611 --> 01:26:52.479
and he just spilled
green sauce all over it.

1912
01:26:52.547 --> 01:26:55.883
Just completely ruined
the shirt, like a little kid.

1913
01:26:55.950 --> 01:26:57.752
And he still
wears it sometimes,

1914
01:26:57.819 --> 01:26:59.887
even with all the stains,
'cause I got it for him.

1915
01:27:02.190 --> 01:27:04.224
He doesn't know
who I am, Gabriel.

1916
01:27:04.291 --> 01:27:05.960
He just thinks
I'm some random rich guy

1917
01:27:06.027 --> 01:27:08.295
that gave him a bunch of money
and got him a house.

1918
01:27:08.361 --> 01:27:09.964
Why did he let you do that?

1919
01:27:10.031 --> 01:27:13.134
I told him he won a contest
'cause he had a cool mustache.

1920
01:27:13.201 --> 01:27:14.401
-Oh.
-(BOTH CHUCKLING)

1921
01:27:18.072 --> 01:27:20.975
-I like this, too.
-What?

1922
01:27:21.042 --> 01:27:23.845
Being with you, laughing.

1923
01:27:23.911 --> 01:27:26.914
It's one of the best parts
of being human.

1924
01:27:26.981 --> 01:27:28.248
It is.

1925
01:27:30.084 --> 01:27:34.254
I just wish
you had a different angel.

1926
01:27:34.321 --> 01:27:36.791
Azrael would never
have let this happen.

1927
01:27:36.858 --> 01:27:38.358
Who's he?

1928
01:27:38.425 --> 01:27:43.831
(SIGHS) He's a great angel,
has giant wings, guides people.

1929
01:27:43.898 --> 01:27:46.000
-He's a rock star.
-(MUTTERS DISMISSIVELY)

1930
01:27:46.067 --> 01:27:48.870
I think I'd rather
have the guy that's
really into cumbia,

1931
01:27:48.936 --> 01:27:50.705
chicken nuggies
and psychedelics.

1932
01:27:50.772 --> 01:27:53.107
You're just saying that
'cause I'm right here.

1933
01:27:54.108 --> 01:27:56.110
Nope.

1934
01:27:56.177 --> 01:27:58.212
I'm saying it
'cause it's true.

1935
01:27:58.880 --> 01:28:00.648
You're my angel.

1936
01:28:00.715 --> 01:28:02.850
And you're not Azrael.
You're Gabriel.

1937
01:28:02.917 --> 01:28:05.352
And you know what?
I love Gabriel.

1938
01:28:05.418 --> 01:28:06.754
I prefer Gabriel.

1939
01:28:09.223 --> 01:28:10.658
And I'm not Jeff.

1940
01:28:10.725 --> 01:28:12.459
I'm Arj.

1941
01:28:12.527 --> 01:28:14.427
And things aren't
going well right now,

1942
01:28:15.630 --> 01:28:17.231
but I got to try.

1943
01:28:17.297 --> 01:28:19.332
I want to see
where it goes, as me.

1944
01:28:20.868 --> 01:28:22.302
As Arj.

1945
01:28:26.941 --> 01:28:29.010
I think
my life's worth living.

1946
01:28:32.947 --> 01:28:33.981
MAN: <i>Hey, yo.</i>

1947
